(window.STEP_BOOK = window.STEP_BOOK || {})["C5"] = {"n":5,"level":"B2+","t":"Argument, Summary and STEP Exam Mastery","lessons":[{"id":"5.1","t":"Argumentative Writing and Counter-Arguments","html":"<p><strong>Unit 5 · Lesson 5.1 · CEFR B2+ · STEP link: Composition Analysis (10%)</strong></p>\n<h3>Objectives</h3>\n<p>1. Build an argument that presents, concedes and rebuts opposing views.</p>\n<p>2. Choose the best rebuttal, concession transition and argumentative conclusion.</p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><strong><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">الأهداف</span></strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">١. أن يبني الطالب حجة تعرض الآراء المقابلة وتسلّم ببعضها وترد عليها.</span></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">٢. أن يختار أفضل رد وأداة تسليم وخاتمة جدلية.</span></p>\n<h3>The Skill</h3>\n<p>An ARGUMENTATIVE essay tries to persuade the reader. A strong argument does not ignore the other side; it uses a three-step pattern. (1) PRESENT the opposing view fairly: Some people argue that … / Critics claim that … / It is often argued that … (2) CONCEDE what is true about it: Admittedly, … / Granted, … / It is true that … / While it is true that … (3) REBUT it with a stronger point and evidence: However, … / Nevertheless, … / Even so, … / In reality, … / Yet … This makes the writer look fair, informed and convincing.</p>\n<p>A REBUTTAL must answer the specific claim, not just repeat the writer's opinion. If critics say renewable energy is too expensive, the rebuttal must talk about cost (the price of solar panels has fallen dramatically). If people say tourism damages culture, the rebuttal must show how tourism can preserve culture. A rebuttal that changes the subject is weak.</p>\n<p>Argumentative conclusions weigh the evidence and restate the position firmly: On balance, … / Ultimately, … / For these reasons, … / Therefore, … They may give a recommendation, but they do not introduce new arguments. Be careful with concession grammar: although / while + clause; despite / in spite of + noun; admittedly and granted begin a sentence followed by a comma; nevertheless, nonetheless and even so follow a full stop or semicolon.</p>\n<p><strong>Examples:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>present</strong> Critics claim that renewable energy is too expensive.</p>\n<p><strong>concede</strong> Admittedly, the initial cost of solar farms is high.</p>\n<p><strong>rebut</strong> Nevertheless, the cost of solar panels has fallen dramatically in the past decade.</p>\n<p><strong>while it is true</strong> While it is true that online classes are convenient, they cannot fully replace learning with classmates.</p>\n<p><strong>✗ weak rebuttal</strong> Critics say it is expensive. However, I think it is good. (does not answer the cost argument)</p>\n<p><strong>✓ strong rebuttal</strong> Critics say it is expensive. However, it saves money over time because fuel is free.</p>\n<p><strong>conclusion</strong> On balance, the advantages of school uniforms clearly outweigh their disadvantages.</p>\n<p><strong>conclusion</strong> Ultimately, AI should support teachers rather than replace them.</p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><strong><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">المهارة</span></strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">المقال الجدلي يحاول إقناع القارئ، والحجة القوية لا تتجاهل الرأي الآخر بل تتبع ثلاث خطوات: عرض الرأي المقابل بإنصاف (Some people argue that)، ثم التسليم بما فيه من صواب (Admittedly / It is true that)، ثم الرد بنقطة أقوى ودليل (However / Nevertheless / In reality). ويجب أن يرد الرد على الادعاء نفسه لا أن يكرر رأي الكاتب فقط. وتوازن الخاتمة الجدلية بين الأدلة وتعيد الموقف بثبات (On balance / Ultimately) دون حجج جديدة.</span></p>\n<h3>Strategy</h3>\n<blockquote>\n<p>1. Identify the opposing claim exactly (cost, freedom, culture, effectiveness).</p>\n<p>2. Choose a rebuttal that answers THAT claim with a stronger point or evidence.</p>\n<p>3. Use concession words correctly: Admittedly, / Granted, + sentence; although / while + clause; despite + noun.</p>\n<p>4. For conclusions, choose an option that weighs the evidence and restates the position (On balance, Ultimately).</p>\n<p>5. Reject options that change the subject or simply add a neutral fact.</p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">حدد الادعاء المقابل بدقة، واختر ردًا يجيب عنه بنقطة أقوى أو دليل، واستخدم أدوات التسليم بقواعدها الصحيحة، واختر للخاتمة بديلًا يوازن الأدلة ويعيد الموقف، وارفض البدائل التي تغير الموضوع أو تضيف حقيقة محايدة.</span></p>\n</blockquote>\n<h3>Traps and Common Mistakes</h3>\n<blockquote>\n<p>✗ A 'rebuttal' that does not answer the specific claim.</p>\n<p>✗ A neutral fact offered as a rebuttal or conclusion.</p>\n<p>✗ A concession word used as a result word (Admittedly, … therefore).</p>\n<p>✗ although / while followed by a noun, or despite followed by a clause.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<h3>Worked STEP Examples (not counted in the quiz)</h3>\n<p><strong>Example 1. Which sentence best REBUTS this argument?</strong></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Some people argue that AI will soon replace teachers. ______ Machines cannot inspire students, understand their feelings or guide them through personal challenges.</p>\n<p>A. AI is becoming more powerful every year.</p>\n<p>B. However, teaching involves much more than delivering information.</p>\n<p>C. Many teachers use computers in class.</p>\n<p>D. Students learn many subjects at school.</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> The claim: AI will replace teachers.</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> A rebuttal must show why that is not true; the next sentence lists what machines cannot do.</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> 'teaching involves much more than delivering information' answers the claim and leads into those points.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>Answer: B</strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">الرد يجب أن يعالج الادعاء نفسه ويمهد للأدلة.</span></p>\n<p><strong>Example 2. Which word or phrase best fills the blank?</strong></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>______, the new law may be difficult to enforce at first; even so, it is an important step towards safer roads.</p>\n<p>A. Therefore B. For example C. Furthermore D. Admittedly</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> The first part admits a weakness (difficult to enforce).</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> The second part (even so) rebuts it.</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> A concession needs Admittedly.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>Answer: D</strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">الجزء الأول تسليم بضعف، فنستخدم Admittedly.</span></p>\n<p><strong>Example 3. Which sentence best concludes this argument?</strong></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Critics argue that space exploration wastes money that could be used to solve problems on Earth. However, space research has produced technologies such as weather satellites, GPS and medical imaging. It also inspires young people to study science. ______</p>\n<p>A. Space exploration, therefore, is an investment in our future rather than a waste of resources.</p>\n<p>B. Space is very large and mostly empty.</p>\n<p>C. Some astronauts have visited the Moon.</p>\n<p>D. Medical imaging is used in hospitals.</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> The paragraph presents a claim (waste of money) and rebuts it with evidence.</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> The conclusion should restate the writer's position firmly.</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> Only the correct answer does this; the distractors are neutral facts.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>Answer: A</strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">الخاتمة الجدلية تعيد الموقف بثبات.</span></p>\n<h3>Writing Task W-B2+-01 — Should artificial intelligence be used to mark student essays?</h3>\n<blockquote>\n<p><strong>Task:</strong> Write an argumentative essay of 250–300 words: Should artificial intelligence be used to mark student essays? Present the opposing view fairly, concede what is true and rebut it with stronger evidence.</p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">اكتب مقالًا جدليًا من مئتين وخمسين إلى ثلاثمئة كلمة: هل يجب استخدام الذكاء الاصطناعي في تصحيح مقالات الطلاب؟ اعرض الرأي المقابل بإنصاف وسلّم بما فيه من صواب ورد عليه بأدلة أقوى.</span></p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>Planning frame</strong></p>\n<p>1. Introduction: hook + background + thesis (AI as assistant, not judge).</p>\n<p>2. Body 1: the supporters' case (speed, consistency, feedback).</p>\n<p>3. Body 2: rebuttal (ideas, argument, personality; teaching to the software; teachers know students).</p>\n<p>4. Body 3: concession + solution (Admittedly … However, combine both).</p>\n<p>5. Conclusion: restate the position firmly.</p>\n<p><strong>Model answer (265 words; target 250–300)</strong></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Imagine handing in an essay and receiving a detailed mark only seconds later. Artificial intelligence (AI) now makes this possible, and some schools are considering using it to assess students' writing. While AI can be a useful assistant, I believe that it should not be the final judge of student essays.</p>\n<p>Supporters of AI marking make several strong points. AI can mark hundreds of essays in minutes, which saves teachers a great deal of time. It is also consistent: unlike a tired human marker, it applies the same criteria to every paper. Furthermore, it can give students instant feedback on grammar and spelling.</p>\n<p>Nevertheless, essays are not simply collections of correct sentences. A good essay presents original ideas, builds a logical argument and shows the writer's personality. These qualities are difficult for a machine to judge fairly. In addition, students may learn to write in a way that pleases the software rather than in a way that communicates clearly. Most importantly, teachers know their students; they can recognize effort, notice progress and give encouragement that motivates young writers.</p>\n<p>Admittedly, teachers' marking is not perfect either, and their time is limited. However, the solution is to combine the strengths of both. AI could check basic accuracy, while teachers focus on ideas, organization and feedback. In this way, students would receive quick corrections as well as thoughtful comments on their thinking.</p>\n<p>In conclusion, AI can support essay marking, but it should not replace teachers. Schools should therefore introduce it carefully, as a tool in teachers' hands. Writing is a human skill, and it deserves a human reader.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>Examiner's commentary</strong></p>\n<p>▸ The opposing view is presented fairly and in detail before it is answered.</p>\n<p>▸ The rebuttal (Nevertheless …) answers the specific claims about speed and consistency with stronger points about ideas and motivation.</p>\n<p>▸ The concession (Admittedly …) followed by a practical solution makes the writer sound reasonable.</p>\n<p>▸ The conclusion restates the position firmly and ends with a memorable final line.</p>\n<p><strong>Self-check before you hand in</strong></p>\n<p>☐ Did I present the opposing view fairly?</p>\n<p>☐ Did I concede at least one valid point (Admittedly / It is true that)?</p>\n<p>☐ Does my rebuttal answer the specific claim with evidence?</p>\n<p>☐ Does my conclusion restate my position without new arguments?</p>\n<p>☐ Is my essay 250–300 words?</p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">تأكد من عرض الرأي المقابل بإنصاف، والتسليم بنقطة صحيحة، والرد عليها بدليل محدد، ومن أن الخاتمة تعيد موقفك.</span></p>","wu":"Worked examples: Example 1 B · Example 2 D · Example 3 A","quiz":[{"l":["Answer all 30 questions. Read each paragraph or sentence carefully and choose the best answer (A, B, C or D).","أجب عن الأسئلة الثلاثين جميعها. اقرأ كل فقرة أو جملة بعناية واختر الإجابة الصحيحة من بين البدائل الأربعة.","Part A — Lesson Focus (Questions 1–20)","الجزء الأول: أسئلة على مهارة الدرس."],"q":[{"n":1,"s":"Which word or phrase best fills the blank?","o":["While it is true","Because it is true","So it is true","Unless it is true"],"x":["______ that online classes are convenient, they cannot fully replace the experience of learning with classmates."],"k":0,"e":"[transition / connector] While it is true — While it is true that … concedes a point before the main claim.","h":"While it is true للتسليم."},{"n":2,"s":"Which sentence best REBUTS this counter-argument?","o":["Junk food is popular with many teenagers.","Some students bring junk food from home.","Freedom of choice is an important value.","However, schools already limit many choices in order to protect students."],"x":["Some people argue that banning junk food in schools restricts students' freedom of choice. ______ After all, schools are responsible for students' health during the school day."],"k":3,"e":"[complete the paragraph] However, schools already limit many choices in order to protect students. — It answers the 'freedom' claim directly.","h":"ترد على ادعاء الحرية."},{"n":3,"s":"Which word or phrase best fills the blank?","o":["Moreover","Consequently","Similarly","Nevertheless"],"x":["Critics claim that renewable energy is too expensive. ______, the cost of solar panels has fallen dramatically in the past decade."],"k":3,"e":"[transition / connector] Nevertheless — The second sentence rebuts the critics' claim.","h":"الجملة الثانية ترد على النقاد."},{"n":4,"s":"Which sentence best concludes this argument?","o":["Uniforms are sold in many shops across the country.","Some students do not like the colour of their uniform.","On balance, the advantages of school uniforms clearly outweigh their disadvantages.","Peer pressure can affect students in many ways."],"x":["Opponents of school uniforms argue that they limit self-expression. Yet uniforms reduce peer pressure, save families money and create a sense of belonging. Students can still express themselves through their ideas, hobbies and achievements. ______"],"k":2,"e":"[concluding sentence] On balance, the advantages of school uniforms clearly outweigh their disadvantages. — On balance weighs both sides and restates the position.","h":"On balance توازن وتعيد الموقف."},{"n":5,"s":"Which word or phrase best fills the blank?","o":["Consequently","Therefore","For instance","Admittedly"],"x":["______, video games can be addictive; however, when played in moderation, they can develop strategic thinking."],"k":3,"e":"[transition / connector] Admittedly — A concession followed by however.","h":"تسليم يليه however."},{"n":6,"s":"Which sentence best REBUTS this argument?","o":["Tourism has grown quickly in recent years.","Many villages are located in the mountains.","In reality, however, tourism can also help to preserve cultural heritage.","Some tourists prefer luxury hotels."],"x":["It is often argued that tourism damages local culture. ______ In many Saudi villages, for example, tourism has encouraged people to restore old houses and revive traditional crafts."],"k":2,"e":"[complete the paragraph] In reality, however, tourism can also help to preserve cultural heritage. — It answers the cultural-damage claim and leads into the example.","h":"ترد على ادعاء الضرر الثقافي."},{"n":7,"s":"Which word or phrase best fills the blank?","o":["as a result","by contrast","for example","in addition"],"x":["Some believe that smartphones should be banned in schools. Others, ______, argue that they can be valuable learning tools when used properly."],"k":1,"e":"[transition / connector] by contrast — Two opposing groups.","h":"مجموعتان متعارضتان."},{"n":8,"s":"Which sentence best fills the blank in the paragraph?","o":["Exams usually take place at the end of the year.","Yet research suggests that long assignments do not necessarily lead to higher marks.","Homework is given in almost every country.","Many parents help their children with homework."],"x":["Some argue that homework is necessary to prepare students for exams. ______ Therefore, the quality of homework matters more than the quantity."],"k":1,"e":"[complete the paragraph] Yet research suggests that long assignments do not necessarily lead to higher marks. — The rebuttal provides evidence that leads to 'Therefore'.","h":"الرد يقدم دليلًا يقود إلى النتيجة."},{"n":9,"s":"Which word or phrase best fills the blank?","o":["Even so","As a result","In other words","For this reason"],"x":["The new policy has some weaknesses. ______, it is a step in the right direction."],"k":0,"e":"[transition / connector] Even so — Even so rebuts the admitted weaknesses.","h":"Even so للرد بعد التسليم."},{"n":10,"s":"Which sentence best concludes this argument?","o":["Zoos are popular with families at weekends.","The Arabian oryx lives in desert areas.","Some animals are difficult to feed.","Therefore, well-managed zoos play a vital role in protecting wildlife."],"x":["Some people believe that zoos are cruel because animals lose their freedom. However, modern zoos protect endangered species, support scientific research and educate millions of visitors. Many species, such as the Arabian oryx, survived only because of breeding programmes in zoos. ______"],"k":3,"e":"[concluding sentence] Therefore, well-managed zoos play a vital role in protecting wildlife. — It restates the position supported by the evidence.","h":"تعيد الموقف المدعوم بالأدلة."},{"n":11,"s":"Which word or phrase best fills the blank?","o":["Because","Unless","Although","So that"],"x":["______ there are some risks, the benefits of vaccination far outweigh them."],"k":2,"e":"[transition / connector] Although — Although + clause concedes the risks.","h":"Although للتسليم."},{"n":12,"s":"Which sentence best fills the blank in the paragraph?","o":["Weekends are important for family time.","Students often travel during long weekends.","Some schools have a six-day week.","This concern, however, is not supported by much evidence."],"x":["Opponents of a four-day school week claim that students will forget what they learn over a longer weekend. ______ In fact, some studies in other countries found no significant drop in achievement."],"k":3,"e":"[complete the paragraph] This concern, however, is not supported by much evidence. — The rebuttal challenges the claim and leads to 'In fact'.","h":"الرد يشكك في الادعاء ويمهد لـ In fact."},{"n":13,"s":"Which word or phrase best fills the blank?","o":["Furthermore","Hence","Likewise","Nonetheless"],"x":["Granted, electric cars are more expensive to buy. ______, they are much cheaper to run and maintain."],"k":3,"e":"[transition / connector] Nonetheless — A rebuttal after the concession Granted.","h":"رد بعد Granted."},{"n":14,"s":"Which sentence best presents the supporters' argument?","o":["Roads are built by large companies.","Traffic is heavy in many cities.","They believe that wider roads allow cars to move more quickly.","Some drivers prefer the metro."],"x":["Many people support building more roads to reduce traffic. ______ However, experts point out that new roads often attract even more cars, so traffic soon returns."],"k":2,"e":"[complete the paragraph] They believe that wider roads allow cars to move more quickly. — The gap explains the supporters' reasoning before However.","h":"الجملة تشرح منطق المؤيدين."},{"n":15,"s":"Which word or phrase best fills the blank?","o":["Conversely","Accordingly","Likewise","Thus"],"x":["Supporters of social media say it connects people. ______, critics point out that it can also make people feel more isolated."],"k":0,"e":"[transition / connector] Conversely — Supporters / critics hold opposite views.","h":"مؤيدون مقابل منتقدين."},{"n":16,"s":"Which sentence best concludes this argument?","o":["Ultimately, AI should support teachers rather than replace them in marking essays.","Multiple-choice tests are common in many exams.","Some teachers mark essays at the weekend.","Creativity is difficult to define."],"x":["Artificial intelligence can mark multiple-choice tests quickly and accurately. However, essays require an understanding of ideas, creativity and argument that machines still find difficult to judge. Teachers also give personal feedback that motivates students. ______"],"k":0,"e":"[concluding sentence] Ultimately, AI should support teachers rather than replace them in marking essays. — Ultimately gives the final, balanced position.","h":"Ultimately للموقف النهائي."},{"n":17,"s":"Which word or phrase best fills the blank?","o":["Therefore","As a result","On the other hand","In other words"],"x":["It is true that the project will be expensive. ______, it will create thousands of jobs and boost the local economy."],"k":2,"e":"[transition / connector] On the other hand — The cost is conceded; the benefits answer it.","h":"التكلفة مسلّم بها والفوائد ترد عليها."},{"n":18,"s":"Which sentence best fills the blank in the paragraph?","o":["English is spoken in many countries.","Arabic is one of the official languages of the United Nations.","Many students study English at school.","However, being bilingual does not mean losing one's first language."],"x":["Some people argue that learning English threatens the Arabic language. ______ Many educated Saudis speak excellent English while remaining proud and skilled users of Arabic."],"k":3,"e":"[complete the paragraph] However, being bilingual does not mean losing one's first language. — The rebuttal answers the claim before the evidence.","h":"الرد يجيب عن الادعاء قبل الدليل."},{"n":19,"s":"Which word or phrase best fills the blank?","o":["moreover","nevertheless","therefore","for example"],"x":["The plan is not perfect; ______, it is the best option currently available."],"k":1,"e":"[transition / connector] nevertheless — not perfect / the best option: concession and rebuttal.","h":"تسليم ثم رد."},{"n":20,"s":"Which sentence best concludes this argument?","o":["Sugary drinks are sold in every supermarket.","For these reasons, a tax on sugary drinks is a fair and effective public health measure.","Some consumers prefer diet drinks.","Hospitals need modern equipment."],"x":["Some economists argue that raising taxes on sugary drinks unfairly punishes consumers. However, such taxes have reduced consumption of sugary drinks in several countries and raised money for health programmes. Since diseases linked to sugar place a heavy burden on hospitals, the long-term savings are considerable. ______"],"k":1,"e":"[concluding sentence] For these reasons, a tax on sugary drinks is a fair and effective public health measure. — It restates the position and answers the 'unfair' claim.","h":"تعيد الموقف وترد على ادعاء الظلم."}]},{"l":["Part B — Mixed STEP Composition Analysis (Questions 21–30)","الجزء الثاني: أسئلة متنوعة من قسم تحليل الكتابة في اختبار STEP."],"q":[{"n":21,"s":"Which sentence does NOT belong in the paragraph?","o":["Sentence 3","Sentence 4","Sentence 5","Sentence 6"],"x":["(1) Artificial intelligence is increasingly used in education. (2) It can create personalized exercises for each student. (3) It can mark simple tests instantly. (4) It can also help teachers identify students who need extra support. (5) Some robots are designed to clean houses. (6) However, it raises concerns about privacy and accuracy. (7) Schools must therefore use AI carefully."],"k":2,"e":"[irrelevant sentence] Sentence 5 — Cleaning robots are not about AI in education.","h":"روبوتات التنظيف خارج الموضوع."},{"n":22,"s":"Which sentence is the best thesis statement for this introduction?","o":["AI tools are developed by technology companies.","Used responsibly, AI can improve students' writing, but it should never replace their own thinking.","Many students use computers at home.","Essays are a common form of assessment."],"x":["AI tools can now check grammar, suggest ideas and even write entire essays. Some educators welcome these tools, while others fear that students will stop thinking for themselves. ______"],"k":1,"e":"[topic sentence / thesis] Used responsibly, AI can improve students' writing, but it should never replace their own thinking. — A clear, balanced, arguable position.","h":"موقف واضح متوازن."},{"n":23,"s":"Choose the best order for the sentences.","o":["2 – 3 – 1 – 4","2 – 1 – 3 – 4","3 – 2 – 1 – 4","2 – 3 – 4 – 1"],"x":["(1) Admittedly, AI may make occasional mistakes when marking.","(2) Many schools are considering using AI to mark student essays.","(3) Supporters argue that it is faster and more consistent than human markers.","(4) Nevertheless, these mistakes can be reduced if teachers review the results."],"k":0,"e":"[best order] 2 – 3 – 1 – 4 — topic → supporters → Admittedly (weakness) → Nevertheless (answer).","h":"موضوع ثم حجة ثم تسليم ثم رد."},{"n":24,"s":"Neither the students (A) nor the teacher (B) were (C) satisfied with (D) the result.","o":["nor","were","satisfied","the"],"k":1,"e":"[error] were — With neither … nor, the verb agrees with the nearer subject (the teacher): was.","h":"الفعل يطابق الأقرب."},{"n":25,"s":"Which sentence is the most appropriate for an academic argument?","o":["Everyone knows exercise makes you smarter.","There is considerable evidence that regular exercise improves academic performance.","Exercise is obviously great for school, right?","It's a fact that sport is the best thing ever for students."],"k":1,"e":"[word choice / register] There is considerable evidence that regular exercise improves academic performance. — Formal and evidence-based, without exaggeration.","h":"رسمية ومبنية على الأدلة."},{"n":26,"s":"Which sentence best fills the blank in the paragraph?","o":["Online learning requires a computer and the internet.","Many universities were founded centuries ago.","Students can study at times that suit them, which is helpful for those with family responsibilities.","Some teachers prefer face-to-face lessons."],"x":["Online learning offers flexibility. ______ It also allows students to review recorded lessons as many times as they need."],"k":2,"e":"[complete the paragraph] Students can study at times that suit them, which is helpful for those with family responsibilities. — The gap explains flexibility before 'It also'.","h":"الجملة تشرح المرونة."},{"n":27,"s":"Which sentence best paraphrases: 'Despite its high cost, the project is likely to pay for itself within ten years.'?","o":["Although the project is expensive, it will probably earn back its cost in a decade.","The project is cheap and will make money immediately.","The project costs too much and will never be profitable.","The project will take ten years to build."],"k":0,"e":"[paraphrase / summary] Although the project is expensive, it will probably earn back its cost in a decade. — Same meaning: expensive, but probably repaid in ten years.","h":"المعنى نفسه بكلمات مختلفة."},{"n":28,"s":"Which sentence is written correctly?","o":["Having considered both sides, the benefits outweigh the risks.","Having considered both sides, it is clear the benefits outweigh the risks to me.","Having considered both sides, the risks are outweighed.","Having considered both sides, I believe that the benefits outweigh the risks."],"k":3,"e":"[error] Having considered both sides, I believe that the benefits outweigh the risks. — I, the person who considered, is the subject.","h":"الفاعل هو من فكّر."},{"n":29,"s":"Which word or phrase best fills the blank?","o":["Inevitably","Conversely","Nonetheless","For instance"],"x":["The city's population is growing rapidly. ______, the demand for water will increase significantly."],"k":0,"e":"[transition / connector] Inevitably — A certain consequence of growth.","h":"نتيجة حتمية."},{"n":30,"s":"Which sentence is the best concluding sentence for the paragraph?","o":["Some employees work at weekends.","Stress can cause health problems.","A shorter working week therefore deserves serious consideration in Saudi Arabia.","Trials are often done by universities."],"x":["Supporters of a shorter working week claim that it improves productivity and well-being. Trials in several countries have shown that employees working four days achieved similar results while feeling less stressed. Although not every job can adapt easily, many companies could benefit. ______"],"k":2,"e":"[concluding sentence] A shorter working week therefore deserves serious consideration in Saudi Arabia. — A measured recommendation based on the evidence.","h":"توصية متزنة مبنية على الأدلة."}]}],"n":30},{"id":"5.2","t":"Paraphrasing and Summarizing","html":"<p><strong>Unit 5 · Lesson 5.2 · CEFR B2+ · STEP link: Composition Analysis (10%)</strong></p>\n<h3>Objectives</h3>\n<p>1. Recognize an accurate paraphrase that keeps the full meaning of the original.</p>\n<p>2. Choose the summary that captures the main idea and key points without minor details or opinions.</p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><strong><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">الأهداف</span></strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">١. أن يتعرف الطالب على إعادة الصياغة الدقيقة التي تحافظ على المعنى الكامل للأصل.</span></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">٢. أن يختار الملخص الذي يتضمن الفكرة الرئيسة والنقاط الأساسية دون تفاصيل ثانوية أو آراء.</span></p>\n<h3>The Skill</h3>\n<p>A PARAPHRASE says the same thing in different words. A good paraphrase keeps ALL the meaning: the same facts, the same degree of certainty (may / will / probably), the same quantity (most / some / all), the same cause and effect, and the same time. It changes the vocabulary (synonyms), the grammar (active ↔︎ passive, noun ↔︎ verb: 'the growth of tourism' → 'tourism has grown') and the sentence structure (although ↔︎ despite). Copying the original with one word changed is not a real paraphrase.</p>\n<p>STEP paraphrase distractors usually change the meaning in one small way. Watch for: (1) CERTAINTY changed (may → will, likely → certain); (2) QUANTITY changed (many → all, some → most); (3) CAUSE reversed (A causes B → B causes A); (4) CONTRAST lost (although A, B → A and B); (5) NEGATIVE added or removed (hardly any → many); (6) an EXTRA idea added that the original never said.</p>\n<p>A SUMMARY gives the main idea and key supporting points in far fewer words. It leaves out examples, numbers that are not essential, repetition and the writer's minor comments, and it never adds the summarizer's own opinion. The best summary of a paragraph usually combines the topic sentence and the overall direction of the support; a weak summary focuses on one detail, adds new information or misrepresents the writer's view.</p>\n<p><strong>Examples:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>original</strong> The number of students studying online has risen sharply since 2020.</p>\n<p><strong>✓ paraphrase</strong> Since 2020, there has been a sharp increase in online learners.</p>\n<p><strong>✗ certainty</strong> Online learning may increase after 2020. (rose = a fact, not a possibility)</p>\n<p><strong>✗ quantity</strong> All students now study online. (the original says nothing about 'all')</p>\n<p><strong>original</strong> Although solar panels are expensive to install, they reduce electricity bills over time.</p>\n<p><strong>✓ paraphrase</strong> Despite their high installation cost, solar panels lower energy bills in the long run.</p>\n<p><strong>✗ contrast lost</strong> Solar panels are expensive and they reduce bills. (the contrast is gone)</p>\n<p><strong>✗ cause reversed</strong> Lower electricity bills make solar panels expensive.</p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><strong><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">المهارة</span></strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">إعادة الصياغة تقول المعنى نفسه بكلمات مختلفة مع الحفاظ على كل المعنى: الحقائق ودرجة اليقين والكمية والسبب والنتيجة والزمن، وتغيّر المفردات والتركيب. ومشتتات STEP تغيّر المعنى تغييرًا صغيرًا: درجة اليقين أو الكمية أو عكس السبب أو حذف التضاد أو إضافة نفي أو إضافة فكرة جديدة. أما الملخص فيعرض الفكرة الرئيسة والنقاط الأساسية بكلمات أقل، دون أمثلة أو أرقام غير ضرورية، ودون إضافة رأي الملخِّص.</span></p>\n<h3>Strategy</h3>\n<blockquote>\n<p>1. Underline the key meaning parts of the original: who, what, how much, how certain, why, when.</p>\n<p>2. Check each option against every part; one wrong part makes the option wrong.</p>\n<p>3. Be suspicious of extreme words (all, always, never, certainly) that were not in the original.</p>\n<p>4. For summaries, find the topic sentence and the overall direction first.</p>\n<p>5. Reject summaries that focus on one example, add opinion or add new information.</p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">ضع خطًا تحت عناصر المعنى في الأصل (من، ماذا، كم، درجة اليقين، لماذا، متى)، وطابق كل بديل مع كل عنصر، واحذر الكلمات المطلقة التي لم ترد في الأصل، وفي الملخص ابحث أولًا عن جملة الموضوع والاتجاه العام، وارفض الملخص الذي يركز على مثال واحد أو يضيف رأيًا أو معلومة جديدة.</span></p>\n</blockquote>\n<h3>Traps and Common Mistakes</h3>\n<blockquote>\n<p>✗ A 'paraphrase' that changes may / might into will / certainly.</p>\n<p>✗ A quantity shift: some → most, many → all.</p>\n<p>✗ Cause and effect reversed.</p>\n<p>✗ A summary built around one example or number.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<h3>Worked STEP Examples (not counted in the quiz)</h3>\n<p><strong>Example 1. Which sentence best paraphrases: 'Experts believe that rising temperatures could reduce crop yields in many regions.'?</strong></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>A. Experts have proved that rising temperatures will destroy all crops.</p>\n<p>B. Crop yields in many regions have caused temperatures to rise.</p>\n<p>C. Experts believe that crop yields are increasing in many regions.</p>\n<p>D. According to specialists, higher temperatures might lower harvests in numerous areas.</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> Key parts: experts believe (opinion), could (possibility), reduce crop yields, many regions.</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> The 'proved … all crops' distractor changes believe → proved, could → will and many → all.</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> Another distractor reverses the cause; the last changes reduce to increase.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>Answer: D</strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">طابق كل عنصر: الاعتقاد، والاحتمال، والكمية، والاتجاه.</span></p>\n<p><strong>Example 2. Which sentence best summarizes this paragraph?</strong></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Desalination plants supply much of the drinking water in the Gulf. However, the process uses large amounts of energy and returns very salty water to the sea, which can harm marine life. Researchers are now testing solar-powered plants and new ways to dilute the waste water.</p>\n<p>A. Desalination provides vital drinking water in the Gulf, but its environmental costs are leading researchers to look for cleaner methods.</p>\n<p>B. Desalination is the only source of water in the Gulf.</p>\n<p>C. Salty waste water harms fish and coral in the sea.</p>\n<p>D. Solar energy is cheaper than any other form of energy.</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> The paragraph has three moves: importance → problem → research.</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> A summary must include all three in general terms.</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> The other options give one detail, exaggerate or add new information.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>Answer: A</strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">الملخص الجيد يغطي اتجاه الفقرة كله.</span></p>\n<p><strong>Example 3. Which sentence best paraphrases: 'Hardly any of the volunteers had previous experience.'?</strong></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>A. Most of the volunteers had previous experience.</p>\n<p>B. None of the volunteers wanted any experience.</p>\n<p>C. Very few of the volunteers had worked in a similar role before.</p>\n<p>D. The volunteers had a lot of experience in other fields.</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> hardly any is a negative quantity (almost none).</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> Most and a lot of reverse the meaning.</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> None … wanted adds a new idea.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>Answer: C</strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">انتبه للنفي المخفي في hardly any.</span></p>\n<h3>Writing Task W-B2+-02 — Summarizing an article on desert solar energy</h3>\n<blockquote>\n<p><strong>Task:</strong> Read the short article below, then write a summary–response of 250–300 words: summarize the article in your own words (about 100 words), then give and support your own view (about 150–200 words).</p>\n<p>Article: 'Saudi Arabia's deserts receive some of the strongest sunlight on Earth. Large solar parks, such as those near Sakaka and in the Eastern Province, already produce electricity for thousands of homes, and many more are planned. Solar power produces no emissions and its costs have fallen sharply. However, dust storms reduce the efficiency of panels, which must be cleaned regularly, often with scarce water. Engineers are developing robot cleaners and water-free cleaning systems. Experts believe that solar energy could provide a large share of the Kingdom's electricity by the 2030s.'</p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">اقرأ المقال القصير ثم اكتب ملخصًا مع رأي من مئتين وخمسين إلى ثلاثمئة كلمة: لخص المقال بكلماتك (نحو مئة كلمة) ثم اعرض رأيك وادعمه (نحو مئة وخمسين إلى مئتي كلمة).</span></p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>Planning frame</strong></p>\n<p>1. Summary sentence 1: source + main idea (According to the article, …).</p>\n<p>2. Summary sentences 2–4: key points (benefits, problem, solutions, forecast) in your own words.</p>\n<p>3. Response introduction: your position.</p>\n<p>4. Response body: two reasons with support.</p>\n<p>5. Conclusion: restate your view.</p>\n<p><strong>Model answer (253 words; target 250–300)</strong></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>According to the article, Saudi Arabia has a natural advantage in solar energy because its deserts receive extremely strong sunlight. Several large solar parks already supply electricity to thousands of households, and more are being built. The writer explains that solar power is clean and has become much cheaper. The main difficulty is dust, which lowers the performance of the panels and means they need frequent cleaning, often with precious water. To solve this, engineers are designing robotic and waterless cleaning methods. Specialists expect solar power to generate a significant part of the country's electricity within the next decade.</p>\n<p>In my view, investing in solar energy is one of the wisest choices the Kingdom can make. Firstly, it makes sense to use a resource that is free and almost unlimited. Oil can be exported or turned into valuable products instead of being burned to produce electricity at home. Secondly, solar power supports the goals of Vision 2030 by creating new industries and jobs for young Saudis, from engineering to maintenance.</p>\n<p>Admittedly, the dust problem is serious, and wasting water in a desert country would be unacceptable. However, the solutions described in the article show that this challenge is technical rather than permanent. As technology improves, cleaning costs will fall, just as the price of panels has already fallen.</p>\n<p>In conclusion, solar energy offers Saudi Arabia a cleaner, cheaper and more independent future. The sun has always been part of life in the desert; now it can also be the source of its power.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>Examiner's commentary</strong></p>\n<p>▸ The summary begins with a reporting phrase (According to the article) and keeps the writer's ideas separate from the response.</p>\n<p>▸ Key points are paraphrased (strong sunlight → extremely strong sunlight; scarce water → precious water; experts believe … could → specialists expect).</p>\n<p>▸ The summary leaves out place names and minor details but keeps every main idea, including the problem and the solution.</p>\n<p>▸ The response has a clear position, two reasons, a concession and a memorable conclusion.</p>\n<p><strong>Self-check before you hand in</strong></p>\n<p>☐ Does my summary start with a reporting phrase?</p>\n<p>☐ Did I use my own words rather than copying sentences?</p>\n<p>☐ Did I include the main idea and all the key points, without my opinion?</p>\n<p>☐ Is my response clearly separated from the summary?</p>\n<p>☐ Is my text 250–300 words?</p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">تأكد من بدء الملخص بعبارة نقل، واستخدام كلماتك، وتغطية النقاط الأساسية دون رأيك، ثم فصل رأيك عن الملخص.</span></p>","wu":"Worked examples: Example 1 D · Example 2 A · Example 3 C","quiz":[{"l":["Answer all 30 questions. Read each paragraph or sentence carefully and choose the best answer (A, B, C or D).","أجب عن الأسئلة الثلاثين جميعها. اقرأ كل فقرة أو جملة بعناية واختر الإجابة الصحيحة من بين البدائل الأربعة.","Part A — Lesson Focus (Questions 1–20)","الجزء الأول: أسئلة على مهارة الدرس."],"q":[{"n":1,"s":"Which sentence best paraphrases: 'The museum attracts more visitors in winter than in summer.'?","o":["More people visit the museum in summer than in winter.","The museum is closed in summer.","The museum attracts visitors only in winter.","Fewer people visit the museum in summer than in winter."],"k":3,"e":"[paraphrase / summary] Fewer people visit the museum in summer than in winter. — more in winter = fewer in summer.","h":"المقارنة نفسها معكوسة الصياغة."},{"n":2,"s":"Which sentence best paraphrases: 'The new metro line has reduced travel time across the city.'?","o":["Journeys across the city have become shorter since the new metro line opened.","The new metro line has increased travel time across the city.","Travel time has caused the new metro line to open.","The new metro line will probably reduce travel time across the city."],"k":0,"e":"[paraphrase / summary] Journeys across the city have become shorter since the new metro line opened. — reduced travel time = journeys are shorter; the tense and certainty are kept.","h":"المعنى والزمن ودرجة اليقين محفوظة."},{"n":3,"s":"Which sentence best paraphrases: 'Most employees prefer flexible working hours.'?","o":["All employees prefer flexible working hours.","A few employees prefer flexible working hours.","Flexible working hours prefer most employees.","The majority of workers would rather have flexible schedules."],"k":3,"e":"[paraphrase / summary] The majority of workers would rather have flexible schedules. — most = the majority; prefer = would rather.","h":"most تعني الأغلبية."},{"n":4,"s":"Which sentence best paraphrases: 'Although the hotel was expensive, the service was excellent.'?","o":["The hotel was expensive because the service was excellent.","Despite the high price of the hotel, the service was outstanding.","The hotel was cheap, and the service was excellent.","The hotel was expensive, so the service was poor."],"k":1,"e":"[paraphrase / summary] Despite the high price of the hotel, the service was outstanding. — Although → Despite; the contrast is kept.","h":"التضاد محفوظ."},{"n":5,"s":"Which sentence best paraphrases: 'The project might be delayed because of bad weather.'?","o":["The project will definitely be delayed by bad weather.","The project caused the bad weather.","Poor weather conditions could cause a delay to the project.","The project was delayed, so the weather was bad."],"k":2,"e":"[paraphrase / summary] Poor weather conditions could cause a delay to the project. — might = could; the cause is kept.","h":"الاحتمال والسبب محفوظان."},{"n":6,"s":"Which sentence best paraphrases: 'Only a small number of applicants were accepted onto the course.'?","o":["Most applicants were accepted onto the course.","No applicants were accepted onto the course.","The course admitted very few of the people who applied.","A small number of courses accepted applicants."],"k":2,"e":"[paraphrase / summary] The course admitted very few of the people who applied. — a small number = very few.","h":"عدد قليل = very few."},{"n":7,"s":"Which sentence best paraphrases: 'The growth of online shopping has forced many small shops to close.'?","o":["Because online shopping has grown, numerous small shops have had to shut down.","Small shops have closed, so online shopping has grown less.","Online shopping may force a few small shops to close in the future.","Many small shops have opened because of online shopping."],"k":0,"e":"[paraphrase / summary] Because online shopping has grown, numerous small shops have had to shut down. — The noun growth becomes the verb has grown; the cause and quantity are kept.","h":"تحويل الاسم إلى فعل مع حفظ المعنى."},{"n":8,"s":"Which sentence best paraphrases: 'It is widely believed that bilingual children develop stronger problem-solving skills.'?","o":["It has been proved that all bilingual children are excellent at solving problems.","Many people think that children who speak two languages become better at solving problems.","Children with strong problem-solving skills usually become bilingual.","A few people believe that bilingual children have weaker problem-solving skills."],"k":1,"e":"[paraphrase / summary] Many people think that children who speak two languages become better at solving problems. — widely believed = many people think; the meaning is not made stronger.","h":"الاعتقاد الشائع لا يصبح حقيقة مثبتة."},{"n":9,"s":"Which sentence best paraphrases: 'The policy was introduced to protect endangered species.'?","o":["Endangered species introduced the policy.","The policy has failed to protect endangered species.","The aim of the policy was to safeguard animals at risk of extinction.","The policy was introduced in spite of endangered species."],"k":2,"e":"[paraphrase / summary] The aim of the policy was to safeguard animals at risk of extinction. — to protect = the aim was to safeguard.","h":"الغرض محفوظ."},{"n":10,"s":"Which sentence best paraphrases: 'Unless the company reduces its costs, it will lose money.'?","o":["The company will make a loss if it does not cut its costs.","The company will lose money because it has reduced its costs.","The company has already lost money and reduced its costs.","If the company cuts its costs, it will certainly lose money."],"k":0,"e":"[paraphrase / summary] The company will make a loss if it does not cut its costs. — unless = if … not.","h":"unless تعني if … not."},{"n":11,"s":"Which sentence best summarizes this paragraph?","o":["Teaching university courses in English brings international advantages, but some fear it may weaken academic Arabic.","Saudi graduates find international jobs easily.","All Saudi universities teach only in English.","Arabic is more important than English at university."],"x":["Many Saudi universities now offer courses entirely in English. This helps graduates compete for international jobs and makes it easier to use global research. However, some educators worry that students may lose confidence in using Arabic for academic purposes."],"k":0,"e":"[paraphrase / summary] Teaching university courses in English brings international advantages, but some fear it may weaken academic Arabic. — It includes the benefit and the concern without adding an opinion.","h":"يذكر الفائدة والقلق دون رأي."},{"n":12,"s":"Which sentence best paraphrases: 'Not until the results were published did the team realize their mistake.'?","o":["The team realized their mistake before the results were published.","The team never realized their mistake.","The results were published because the team made a mistake.","The team only became aware of their error when the results were published."],"k":3,"e":"[paraphrase / summary] The team only became aware of their error when the results were published. — Not until … did = only when.","h":"Not until تعني فقط عندما."},{"n":13,"s":"Which sentence best summarizes this paragraph?","o":["Adequate sleep helps the brain store information, so students who sleep too little may learn less effectively.","Students should sleep exactly seven hours every night.","The brain is very active during the day.","Tests are more difficult for students who study at night."],"x":["Sleep plays a key role in learning. During deep sleep, the brain organizes and stores information gathered during the day. Students who sleep fewer than seven hours often find it harder to remember what they have studied, and their performance in tests may suffer."],"k":0,"e":"[paraphrase / summary] Adequate sleep helps the brain store information, so students who sleep too little may learn less effectively. — The main idea (sleep and learning) and its result.","h":"الفكرة الرئيسة ونتيجتها."},{"n":14,"s":"Which sentence best paraphrases: 'The bridge is too narrow for large lorries to cross.'?","o":["The bridge is not wide enough for big trucks to use.","Large lorries are too narrow to cross the bridge.","The bridge is wide enough for large lorries.","Large lorries have made the bridge narrow."],"k":0,"e":"[paraphrase / summary] The bridge is not wide enough for big trucks to use. — too narrow = not wide enough.","h":"too narrow تعني not wide enough."},{"n":15,"s":"Which sentence best summarizes this paragraph?","o":["Mud walls are the strongest building material.","Najdi houses had small windows and courtyards.","Traditional Najdi houses used clever design to stay cool, and modern architects are reviving these ideas to save energy.","Modern homes in Najd are no longer energy-efficient."],"x":["The traditional Najdi house was designed to suit the hot, dry climate. Thick mud walls kept rooms cool during the day, while small, high windows let in light but little heat. An open courtyard in the centre allowed air to circulate. Today, some architects are using these ideas again to build energy-efficient homes."],"k":2,"e":"[paraphrase / summary] Traditional Najdi houses used clever design to stay cool, and modern architects are reviving these ideas to save energy. — It covers the design purpose and the modern use; it does not list details.","h":"يغطي الهدف والاستخدام الحديث."},{"n":16,"s":"Which sentence best paraphrases: 'The more you practise, the more confident you become.'?","o":["Practising more leads to greater confidence.","Confidence leads people to practise less.","If you practise, you will be confident immediately.","The more confident you become, the less you practise."],"k":0,"e":"[paraphrase / summary] Practising more leads to greater confidence. — the more … the more = more X leads to more Y.","h":"زيادة أحدهما تؤدي إلى زيادة الآخر."},{"n":17,"s":"Which sentence best summarizes this paragraph?","o":["Fast fashion is cheap and fashionable.","Workers in the fashion industry are poorly paid.","Cheap fast fashion has serious environmental and social costs, which is leading some shoppers to change their habits.","Everyone now buys second-hand clothes."],"x":["Fast fashion allows people to buy fashionable clothes at very low prices. However, the industry produces huge amounts of waste, uses large quantities of water and often depends on poorly paid workers. Some consumers are now choosing second-hand clothes or buying fewer, better-quality items."],"k":2,"e":"[paraphrase / summary] Cheap fast fashion has serious environmental and social costs, which is leading some shoppers to change their habits. — It covers the benefit, the costs and the response.","h":"يغطي الفائدة والتكاليف والاستجابة."},{"n":18,"s":"Which sentence best paraphrases: 'The government is expected to announce new regulations next month.'?","o":["The government announced new regulations last month.","The government will definitely not announce new rules.","New regulations have caused the government to make an announcement.","New rules will probably be announced by the government next month."],"k":3,"e":"[paraphrase / summary] New rules will probably be announced by the government next month. — is expected to = will probably; the time is kept.","h":"is expected تعني على الأرجح."},{"n":19,"s":"Which sentence best summarizes this paragraph?","o":["Japan produced the first cultured pearls in the 1930s.","Pearl diving was once a vital but dangerous occupation in the Gulf that declined because of cultured pearls and the discovery of oil.","Pearl divers spent many months at sea.","Oil is more valuable than pearls."],"x":["In the past, pearl diving was the main source of income for many families on the Gulf coast. Divers spent months at sea in dangerous conditions. When cultured pearls from Japan appeared in the 1930s and oil was discovered soon afterwards, the industry quickly declined."],"k":1,"e":"[paraphrase / summary] Pearl diving was once a vital but dangerous occupation in the Gulf that declined because of cultured pearls and the discovery of oil. — The main idea and the two causes of decline.","h":"الفكرة الرئيسة وسببا التراجع."},{"n":20,"s":"Which sentence best paraphrases: 'Had the warning been issued earlier, more people could have left the area.'?","o":["The warning was issued early, so many people left the area.","More people left the area, so the warning was issued.","Because the warning came late, fewer people were able to leave the area.","People will leave the area if a warning is issued."],"k":2,"e":"[paraphrase / summary] Because the warning came late, fewer people were able to leave the area. — A third conditional describes an unreal past: the warning was late.","h":"الشرط الثالث يصف ماضيًا لم يحدث."}]},{"l":["Part B — Mixed STEP Composition Analysis (Questions 21–30)","الجزء الثاني: أسئلة متنوعة من قسم تحليل الكتابة في اختبار STEP."],"q":[{"n":21,"s":"Which reporting verb best shows that the writer strongly disagrees with a claim?","o":["The author mentions the claim that tourism always damages culture.","The author notes the claim that tourism always damages culture.","The author repeats the claim that tourism always damages culture.","The author rejects the claim that tourism always damages culture."],"k":3,"e":"[word choice / register] The author rejects the claim that tourism always damages culture. — rejects shows strong disagreement.","h":"rejects تعني الرفض."},{"n":22,"s":"Which word or phrase best fills the blank?","o":["On the contrary","Even so","Instead","In other words"],"x":["The study found that students who read daily had larger vocabularies. ______, regular reading appears to be an effective way to learn new words."],"k":3,"e":"[transition / connector] In other words — In other words restates the finding.","h":"In other words لإعادة الصياغة."},{"n":23,"s":"The report (A) suggests that (B) the number of cyclists (C) have increased (D) significantly.","o":["suggests","the number","have increased","significantly"],"k":2,"e":"[error] have increased — the number of + plural noun takes a singular verb: has increased.","h":"the number مفرد."},{"n":24,"s":"Which sentence does NOT belong in the paragraph?","o":["Sentence 3","Sentence 4","Sentence 5","Sentence 6"],"x":["(1) Paraphrasing is an essential academic skill. (2) It shows that a student has understood a source. (3) It also helps writers avoid copying other people's words. (4) Many famous writers have published several books. (5) Good paraphrases change both the vocabulary and the structure. (6) However, they must keep the original meaning."],"k":1,"e":"[irrelevant sentence] Sentence 4 — Famous writers' books are not about paraphrasing skills.","h":"الجملة خارج الموضوع."},{"n":25,"s":"Which sentence is the best concluding sentence for the paragraph?","o":["Journalists often write very long articles.","The ability to summarize is therefore valuable both at school and at work.","Managers usually work in large offices.","Some speeches last more than an hour."],"x":["Summaries are useful in many situations. Students use them to review lessons, journalists use them to report long speeches, and managers rely on them to make quick decisions. In each case, a good summary saves time while keeping the essential information. ______"],"k":1,"e":"[concluding sentence] The ability to summarize is therefore valuable both at school and at work. — It draws a general conclusion from the examples.","h":"خلاصة عامة من الأمثلة."},{"n":26,"s":"Choose the best order for the sentences.","o":["2 – 1 – 4 – 3","1 – 2 – 4 – 3","2 – 4 – 1 – 3","2 – 1 – 3 – 4"],"x":["(1) Next, write the main idea in one sentence using your own words.","(2) First, read the text carefully and underline the key points.","(3) Finally, compare your summary with the original to check that nothing important has been changed.","(4) Then add the most important supporting points, leaving out examples and details."],"k":0,"e":"[best order] 2 – 1 – 4 – 3 — First → Next → Then → Finally.","h":"ترتيب الخطوات."},{"n":27,"s":"Which topic sentence best fits this paragraph?","o":["Many students find summaries difficult.","A summary must represent the original text accurately and objectively.","Some texts are very long.","Opinions are important in essays."],"x":["______ It should not include the summarizer's own opinions, new information or minor examples. Instead, it should give the main idea and the key points in a shorter form."],"k":1,"e":"[topic sentence / thesis] A summary must represent the original text accurately and objectively. — It introduces what a summary must and must not include.","h":"تقدم ما يجب أن يتضمنه الملخص."},{"n":28,"s":"Which sentence best paraphrases: 'Rarely have scientists seen such rapid changes in the climate.'?","o":["Scientists often see rapid changes in the climate.","Scientists have seldom observed climate change happening so quickly.","Scientists have never studied the climate.","Rapid climate changes are rarely studied by scientists."],"k":1,"e":"[paraphrase / summary] Scientists have seldom observed climate change happening so quickly. — Rarely have … = have seldom.","h":"Rarely تعني نادرًا."},{"n":29,"s":"Which is the most appropriate way to begin a summary in an academic text?","o":["I totally agree that …","Everybody knows that …","According to the article, …","In my humble opinion, …"],"k":2,"e":"[word choice / register] According to the article, … — A neutral reporting phrase.","h":"عبارة نقل محايدة."},{"n":30,"s":"Which sentence best fills the blank in the paragraph?","o":["Rivers are often polluted by factories.","Some writers prefer short sentences.","Pollution is a serious global problem.","It often changes the grammar of the sentence as well, such as from active to passive."],"x":["A good paraphrase changes more than just a few words. ______ For example, 'Pollution damaged the river' could become 'The river was damaged by pollution'."],"k":3,"e":"[complete the paragraph] It often changes the grammar of the sentence as well, such as from active to passive. — The example shows an active-to-passive change.","h":"المثال يوضح التحويل إلى المبني للمجهول."}]}],"n":30},{"id":"5.3","t":"Advanced Editing in Context","html":"<p><strong>Unit 5 · Lesson 5.3 · CEFR B2+ · STEP link: Composition Analysis (10%)</strong></p>\n<h3>Objectives</h3>\n<p>1. Identify advanced grammar, word-form and usage errors in academic sentences.</p>\n<p>2. Edit a full essay for accuracy, consistency and clarity.</p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><strong><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">الأهداف</span></strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">١. أن يحدد الطالب الأخطاء المتقدمة في القواعد وصيغ الكلمات والاستخدام في الجمل الأكاديمية.</span></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">٢. أن يحرر مقالًا كاملًا من حيث الدقة والاتساق والوضوح.</span></p>\n<h3>The Skill</h3>\n<p>At B2+ level, STEP error questions test language that looks correct at first glance. The most frequent areas are: AGREEMENT with distant or tricky subjects (each of … is; the number of … has; neither of … is; the report, together with the tables, was); TENSE SEQUENCE (past perfect for the earlier past action; reported speech backshift); and WORD FORM (practical / practically / practicality; temperature, not temperate).</p>\n<p>Other common areas are: PARALLELISM in lists and pairs (to reduce, encourage and raise); FIXED PREPOSITIONS and verbs that take no preposition (discuss the results, not discuss about; despite the cost, not despite of); COUNT and NONCOUNT nouns (a number of people, an amount of money); COMPARATIVES (the less …, the healthier …); INDIRECT QUESTIONS with statement word order (asked me where I had put …); and DANGLING MODIFIERS (Having been closed for months, the museum …).</p>\n<p>Edit in context: read the WHOLE sentence first, find the main subject and verb, then check each underlined part against its partner (subject ↔︎ verb, pronoun ↔︎ noun, list item ↔︎ list item, preposition ↔︎ verb). Most sentences contain exactly one error, and the other three underlined parts are there to distract you; if you cannot find an error, check the agreement again.</p>\n<p><strong>Examples:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>agreement</strong> Each of the proposals ✗were → ✓was reviewed carefully.</p>\n<p><strong>number/amount</strong> A growing ✗amount → ✓number of people prefer to shop online.</p>\n<p><strong>tense</strong> When the manager entered, the employees ✗have already started → ✓had already started.</p>\n<p><strong>parallelism</strong> to reduce waste, encourage recycling and ✗raising → ✓raise awareness</p>\n<p><strong>preposition</strong> ✗Despite of → ✓Despite the high cost, … ✗discuss about → ✓discuss the results</p>\n<p><strong>comparative</strong> The less sugar you eat, ✗the healthiest → ✓the healthier your teeth will be.</p>\n<p><strong>indirect question</strong> He asked me where ✗did I put → ✓I had put the files.</p>\n<p><strong>word form</strong> too expensive and ✗not practically → ✓impractical</p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><strong><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">المهارة</span></strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">في مستوى فوق المتوسط المتقدم تختبر أسئلة الخطأ لغةً تبدو صحيحة للوهلة الأولى، وأشهر مجالاتها: المطابقة مع الفاعل البعيد (each of … is / the number of … has)، وتسلسل الأزمنة (الماضي التام للحدث الأسبق)، وصيغ الكلمات، والتوازي، وحروف الجر الثابتة (discuss دون about، despite دون of)، والمعدود وغير المعدود (number / amount)، وصيغ المقارنة (the less … the healthier)، والسؤال غير المباشر بترتيب الجملة الخبرية، والمعدِّل المعلق. اقرأ الجملة كاملة وحدد الفاعل والفعل ثم طابق كل جزء مسطّر مع ما يرتبط به.</span></p>\n<h3>Strategy</h3>\n<blockquote>\n<p>1. Read the whole sentence before looking at the underlined parts.</p>\n<p>2. Find the true subject: ignore 'of …' phrases, relative clauses and 'together with …'.</p>\n<p>3. Check time words (when, by the time, since, ago) against the tenses.</p>\n<p>4. Check every list for parallel forms and every verb for its correct preposition (or no preposition).</p>\n<p>5. If nothing looks wrong, check word form (noun / adjective / adverb) and count / noncount nouns.</p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">اقرأ الجملة كاملة أولًا، وحدد الفاعل الحقيقي متجاهلًا العبارات الفاصلة، وطابق ظروف الزمن مع الأفعال، وافحص التوازي في القوائم وحروف الجر بعد الأفعال، وإذا لم تجد خطأ فافحص صيغة الكلمة والمعدود وغير المعدود.</span></p>\n</blockquote>\n<h3>Traps and Common Mistakes</h3>\n<blockquote>\n<p>✗ Making the verb agree with the nearest noun instead of the true subject.</p>\n<p>✗ Thinking a long, formal-looking phrase must be correct.</p>\n<p>✗ Missing a word-form error because the meaning is clear.</p>\n<p>✗ Choosing a correct but unusual structure (for example, inversion) as the error.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<h3>Worked STEP Examples (not counted in the quiz)</h3>\n<p><strong>Example 1. The report, (A) <u>together with</u> the attached tables, (B) <u>were</u> sent (C) <u>to</u> the director (D) <u>yesterday</u>.</strong></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>A. together with B. were C. to D. yesterday</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> Find the subject: The report.</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> together with the attached tables is extra information between commas.</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> A singular subject needs was, so B is wrong.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>Answer: B</strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">تجاهل العبارة الفاصلة وابحث عن الفاعل الحقيقي.</span></p>\n<p><strong>Example 2. The students (A) <u>were</u> (B) <u>surprised</u> to learn that the museum (C) <u>has been built</u> more than a century (D) <u>earlier</u>.</strong></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>A. were B. surprised C. has been built D. earlier</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> The main verb is in the past: were surprised to learn.</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> The building took place before that, and earlier confirms it.</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> Past perfect is needed: had been built.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>Answer: C</strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">الماضي التام للحدث الأسبق.</span></p>\n<p><strong>Example 3. Which sentence is written correctly?</strong></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>A. Only after the results had been checked the team published them.</p>\n<p>B. Only after the results had been checked did the team publish them.</p>\n<p>C. Only after the results had been checked did the team published them.</p>\n<p>D. Only after the results had been checked, did published the team them.</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> Only after … at the beginning of a sentence requires inversion.</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> Inversion uses did + subject + base verb (did the team publish).</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> One distractor has no inversion; the others use the wrong verb form or word order.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>Answer: B</strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">بعد Only after نستخدم did + الفاعل + المصدر.</span></p>\n<h3>Writing Task W-B2+-03 — Editing and rewriting an essay on food waste</h3>\n<blockquote>\n<p><strong>Task:</strong> Write a problem–solution essay of 250–300 words: 'Food waste in Saudi homes and restaurants'. Explain the problem and its causes, propose at least two solutions, then edit your draft using the Lesson 5.3 checklist (agreement, tenses, parallelism, prepositions, word form).</p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">اكتب مقالًا من مئتين وخمسين إلى ثلاثمئة كلمة بنمط المشكلة والحل عن هدر الطعام في البيوت والمطاعم السعودية، واشرح المشكلة وأسبابها، واقترح حلين على الأقل، ثم حرر مسودتك باستخدام قائمة الدرس.</span></p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>Planning frame</strong></p>\n<p>1. Introduction: hook + the size of the problem + thesis.</p>\n<p>2. Body 1: causes (generosity and large portions, poor planning, restaurant buffets).</p>\n<p>3. Body 2: solution 1 (families: planning, storing, sharing).</p>\n<p>4. Body 3: solution 2 (restaurants and the government: smaller portions, donations, awareness).</p>\n<p>5. Conclusion: restate and call to action.</p>\n<p><strong>Model answer (253 words; target 250–300)</strong></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Every evening, large quantities of perfectly good rice, bread and meat are thrown away across the Kingdom. Food waste has become a serious problem in Saudi Arabia, and it costs families, businesses and the environment a great deal. Fortunately, the problem can be greatly reduced if households, restaurants and the authorities work together.</p>\n<p>The causes of the problem are partly cultural. Generosity is an important value in our culture, so hosts often prepare far more food than their guests can eat. In addition, many families shop without a list and buy more than they need, while restaurants that offer large buffets inevitably throw away the dishes that remain at the end of the day.</p>\n<p>The first solution lies in the home. Families can plan their meals for the week, store leftovers properly and turn them into new dishes. Generous hosts do not need to waste food; instead, they can share what remains with neighbours, workers or charities.</p>\n<p>The second solution involves restaurants and the government. Restaurants could serve smaller portions, offer boxes for leftovers and donate unsold food to food banks such as Ita'am. Meanwhile, national campaigns can remind people that wasting food is neither generous nor responsible, and schools can teach children to value what they eat.</p>\n<p>In conclusion, food waste is a problem that has been growing for years, but it is not impossible to solve. If every family and every restaurant makes small changes, the Kingdom can protect its resources, help those in need and remain generous without being wasteful.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>Examiner's commentary</strong></p>\n<p>▸ The essay follows a clear problem–solution structure with one main idea in each paragraph.</p>\n<p>▸ Editing points: the number of …; parallel lists (plan …, store … and turn …); neither … nor; past and present tenses kept consistent.</p>\n<p>▸ Cohesion devices (In addition, instead, Meanwhile) guide the reader.</p>\n<p>▸ The conclusion links back to the cultural cause with a memorable final phrase: generous without being wasteful.</p>\n<p><strong>Self-check before you hand in</strong></p>\n<p>☐ Do all my verbs agree with their true subjects?</p>\n<p>☐ Are my tenses consistent and logical?</p>\n<p>☐ Are my lists parallel?</p>\n<p>☐ Did I use the correct prepositions (and no extra ones)?</p>\n<p>☐ Is my essay 250–300 words?</p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">حرر مقالك: المطابقة بين الفاعل والفعل، واتساق الأزمنة، والتوازي، وحروف الجر، وصيغ الكلمات.</span></p>","wu":"Worked examples: Example 1 B · Example 2 C · Example 3 B","quiz":[{"l":["Answer all 30 questions. Read each paragraph or sentence carefully and choose the best answer (A, B, C or D).","أجب عن الأسئلة الثلاثين جميعها. اقرأ كل فقرة أو جملة بعناية واختر الإجابة الصحيحة من بين البدائل الأربعة.","Part A — Lesson Focus (Questions 1–20)","الجزء الأول: أسئلة على مهارة الدرس."],"q":[{"n":1,"s":"Each of the proposals (A) submitted by the students (B) were reviewed (C) carefully by (D) the committee.","o":["submitted","were","carefully","the"],"k":1,"e":"[error] were — Each of … is singular: was reviewed.","h":"Each مفرد."},{"n":2,"s":"(A) The research, (B) which was published last year, (C) suggest that (D) regular exercise improves memory.","o":["The","which","suggest","regular"],"k":2,"e":"[error] suggest — The subject research is singular: suggests.","h":"research مفرد."},{"n":3,"s":"(A) Despite of the high cost, the government (B) decided to (C) build the new (D) hospital.","o":["Despite of","decided","build","hospital"],"k":0,"e":"[error] Despite of — despite takes no of: Despite the high cost.","h":"despite بلا of."},{"n":4,"s":"The new policy aims (A) to reduce waste, (B) encourage recycling and (C) raising awareness (D) among residents.","o":["to reduce","encourage","raising","among"],"k":2,"e":"[error] raising — Parallel base verbs: to reduce, encourage and raise.","h":"التوازي: raise."},{"n":5,"s":"When the manager (A) entered the room, the employees (B) have already started the meeting (C) without (D) him.","o":["entered","have already started","without","him"],"k":1,"e":"[error] have already started — The earlier past action needs the past perfect: had already started.","h":"الماضي التام للأسبق."},{"n":6,"s":"The number of visitors to AlUla (A) have risen (B) sharply (C) since the new airport (D) opened.","o":["have","sharply","since","opened"],"k":0,"e":"[error] have — The number of … is singular: has risen.","h":"The number مفرد."},{"n":7,"s":"The article compares online learning (A) with classroom learning and (B) concludes that both (C) have (D) advantage.","o":["with","concludes","have","advantage"],"k":3,"e":"[error] advantage — both … have advantages (plural countable noun).","h":"advantages جمع."},{"n":8,"s":"A growing (A) amount of people (B) prefer to shop online (C) because it saves (D) time.","o":["amount","prefer","because","time"],"k":0,"e":"[error] amount — people is countable: a growing number of.","h":"people معدود: number."},{"n":9,"s":"The less sugar you (A) eat, (B) the healthiest your teeth (C) will (D) be.","o":["eat","the healthiest","will","be"],"k":1,"e":"[error] the healthiest — the less …, the + comparative: the healthier.","h":"صيغة المقارنة: the healthier."},{"n":10,"s":"The manager asked me where (A) I (B) had put the files and (C) why (D) was I late.","o":["I","had put","why","was I"],"k":3,"e":"[error] was I — Indirect questions use statement order: why I was late.","h":"السؤال غير المباشر بترتيب الخبر."},{"n":11,"s":"(A) Discussing about the results in small groups (B) helped the students (C) understand (D) them better.","o":["Discussing about","helped","understand","them"],"k":0,"e":"[error] Discussing about — discuss takes no preposition: Discussing the results.","h":"discuss بلا about."},{"n":12,"s":"Having (A) been closed for (B) repairs for six months, (C) visitors were delighted when the museum (D) reopened.","o":["been","repairs","visitors","reopened"],"k":2,"e":"[error] visitors — The visitors were not closed (a dangling modifier): the museum delighted visitors when it reopened.","h":"الزوار لم يُغلقوا."},{"n":13,"s":"The professor explained that the experiment (A) had failed because the samples (B) had been (C) stored at the wrong (D) temperate.","o":["had failed","had been","stored","temperate"],"k":3,"e":"[error] temperate — The noun is temperature; temperate is an adjective.","h":"temperature اسم."},{"n":14,"s":"(A) Despite the heavy rain, the match (B) continuing as (C) planned (D) by the organizers.","o":["Despite","continuing","planned","by"],"k":1,"e":"[error] continuing — The sentence needs a main verb: the match continued.","h":"الجملة تحتاج فعلًا رئيسًا."},{"n":15,"s":"The proposal was (A) rejected (B) because it was (C) too expensive and (D) not practically.","o":["rejected","because","too","not practically"],"k":3,"e":"[error] not practically — Parallel adjectives: too expensive and impractical.","h":"صفتان متوازيتان."},{"n":16,"s":"Which sentence is punctuated correctly?","o":["My brother who lives in Jeddah, works as an engineer.","My brother, who lives in Jeddah works as an engineer.","My brother, who lives in Jeddah, works as an engineer.","My brother who, lives in Jeddah, works as an engineer."],"k":2,"e":"[error] My brother, who lives in Jeddah, works as an engineer. — A non-defining relative clause needs a comma on both sides.","h":"الجملة الوصفية غير المحددة بين فاصلتين."},{"n":17,"s":"Which sentence contains NO error?","o":["Neither of the two solutions are completely satisfactory.","Neither of the two solution is completely satisfactory.","Neither of the two solutions is completely satisfactory.","Neither of the two solutions is complete satisfactory."],"k":2,"e":"[error] Neither of the two solutions is completely satisfactory. — Neither of + plural noun + singular verb; adverb before an adjective.","h":"Neither of مع فعل مفرد."},{"n":18,"s":"Which sentence has clear pronoun reference?","o":["When Saad met Fahad, he told him about his new job.","When Saad met Fahad, Saad told him about the new job.","Saad told Fahad that he had got his new job.","When Saad met Fahad, he said he had got the job he wanted."],"k":1,"e":"[error] When Saad met Fahad, Saad told him about the new job. — Only the first makes clear who is speaking.","h":"الضمير واضح المرجع."},{"n":19,"s":"Which sentence uses the correct sequence of tenses?","o":["She said that she has finished the report yesterday.","She said that she finishes the report the day before.","She said that she had finished the report the day before.","She says that she had finished the report tomorrow."],"k":2,"e":"[error] She said that she had finished the report the day before. — Reported speech: past → past perfect; yesterday → the day before.","h":"تحويل الكلام المنقول."},{"n":20,"s":"Which sentence is correct?","o":["It is essential that every applicant submits the form before the deadline yesterday.","It is essential that every applicant submit the form before the deadline.","It is essential that every applicant to submit the form before the deadline.","It is essential that every applicant submitting the form before the deadline."],"k":1,"e":"[error] It is essential that every applicant submit the form before the deadline. — It is essential that + subject + base verb (subjunctive).","h":"بعد It is essential that المصدر."}]},{"l":["Part B — Mixed STEP Composition Analysis (Questions 21–30)","الجزء الثاني: أسئلة متنوعة من قسم تحليل الكتابة في اختبار STEP."],"q":[{"n":21,"s":"Which word or phrase best fills the blank?","o":["Moreover","In contrast","Otherwise","Instead"],"x":["Food waste costs families money. ______, it harms the environment, because rotting food produces greenhouse gases."],"k":0,"e":"[transition / connector] Moreover — Moreover adds a second problem.","h":"Moreover للإضافة."},{"n":22,"s":"The government, (A) as well as several charities, (B) are working (C) to reduce food waste (D) across the Kingdom.","o":["as well as","are","to reduce","across"],"k":1,"e":"[error] are — The subject is The government: is working.","h":"الفاعل مفرد."},{"n":23,"s":"Which sentence best paraphrases: 'Around a third of all food produced worldwide is wasted.'?","o":["A third of the world's population wastes food.","Exactly thirty per cent of food is wasted in every country.","Most of the food produced worldwide is wasted.","Roughly one in every three portions of food made globally is thrown away."],"k":3,"e":"[paraphrase / summary] Roughly one in every three portions of food made globally is thrown away. — around a third = roughly one in three.","h":"نحو الثلث."},{"n":24,"s":"Which sentence does NOT belong in the paragraph?","o":["Sentence 3","Sentence 4","Sentence 5","Sentence 6"],"x":["(1) Editing is the final stage of the writing process. (2) Writers check grammar, spelling and punctuation. (3) They also make sure the tenses are consistent. (4) Good editors read their work slowly, sentence by sentence. (5) Many novels are later turned into films. (6) Some writers read their essays aloud to hear the mistakes."],"k":2,"e":"[irrelevant sentence] Sentence 5 — Films made from novels are not about editing.","h":"الجملة خارج الموضوع."},{"n":25,"s":"Which word best completes the formal sentence: 'The new regulations will ______ restaurants to report the amount of food they throw away.'?","o":["make up","let on","get round","require"],"k":3,"e":"[word choice / register] require — require = officially oblige.","h":"require تعني يُلزم."},{"n":26,"s":"Choose the best order for the sentences.","o":["2 – 4 – 1 – 3","2 – 1 – 4 – 3","4 – 2 – 1 – 3","2 – 4 – 3 – 1"],"x":["(1) Then check that each verb agrees with its subject.","(2) First, read your essay once for meaning and organization.","(3) Finally, look for spelling and punctuation mistakes.","(4) Next, look at your tenses and make sure they are consistent."],"k":0,"e":"[best order] 2 – 4 – 1 – 3 — First → Next → Then → Finally.","h":"ترتيب خطوات التحرير."},{"n":27,"s":"Which sentence is the best concluding sentence for the paragraph?","o":["These initiatives show that reducing food waste can be both practical and profitable.","Riyadh has many restaurants and supermarkets.","Fruit and vegetables are healthy.","Mobile apps are popular with young people."],"x":["Many restaurants in Riyadh now donate unsold meals to charities. Some supermarkets sell fruit and vegetables that are slightly damaged at lower prices. Mobile apps also connect people with shops that have surplus food at the end of the day. ______"],"k":0,"e":"[concluding sentence] These initiatives show that reducing food waste can be both practical and profitable. — A general conclusion drawn from the three examples.","h":"خلاصة من الأمثلة."},{"n":28,"s":"Which topic sentence best fits this paragraph?","o":["Hotels employ many chefs.","Buffets usually offer a wide variety of dishes.","Restaurants are busy during holidays.","Open buffets encourage diners to take more food than they need."],"x":["______ When they take more than they can eat and leave the rest, the restaurant has no choice but to throw the food away. Hotels in particular report that buffets produce the largest share of their waste."],"k":3,"e":"[topic sentence / thesis] Open buffets encourage diners to take more food than they need. — It states the cause explained in the details.","h":"يذكر السبب الذي تشرحه التفاصيل."},{"n":29,"s":"If families (A) planned their meals more carefully, they (B) will (C) throw away (D) much less food.","o":["planned","will","throw","much"],"k":1,"e":"[error] will — The second conditional needs would: they would throw away.","h":"الشرط الثاني: would."},{"n":30,"s":"Which sentence best fills the blank in the paragraph?","o":["Food prices have increased in recent years.","Some families eat in restaurants every weekend.","Supermarkets are open late at night.","One simple solution is to keep a record of everything that is thrown away for a week."],"x":["Many people do not realize how much food they waste. ______ The results often surprise them and motivate them to change."],"k":3,"e":"[complete the paragraph] One simple solution is to keep a record of everything that is thrown away for a week. — The results refers to the record.","h":"The results تعود إلى السجل."}]}],"n":30},{"id":"5.4","t":"Timed Writing Production","html":"<p><strong>Unit 5 · Lesson 5.4 · CEFR B2+ · STEP link: Composition Analysis (10%)</strong></p>\n<h3>Objectives</h3>\n<p>1. Plan, write and check a 250–300-word essay within 40 minutes.</p>\n<p>2. Make fast, accurate decisions about thesis, organization, cohesion and accuracy under time pressure.</p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><strong><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">الأهداف</span></strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">١. أن يخطط الطالب ويكتب ويراجع مقالًا من مئتين وخمسين إلى ثلاثمئة كلمة في أربعين دقيقة.</span></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">٢. أن يتخذ قرارات سريعة ودقيقة بشأن الأطروحة والتنظيم والترابط والدقة تحت ضغط الوقت.</span></p>\n<h3>The Skill</h3>\n<p>Timed writing is a race against the clock, so you need a fixed routine. A useful plan for 40 minutes is: 5 minutes to ANALYZE and PLAN (underline the key words in the question, decide your position, note two or three reasons and one counter-argument); 28 minutes to WRITE (introduction about 3 minutes, each body paragraph about 7 minutes, conclusion about 3 minutes); and 7 minutes to CHECK (agreement, tenses, articles, spelling, punctuation).</p>\n<p>Under time pressure, the most common problems are: (1) not answering the exact question (writing about technology in general when the question asks about remote WORK); (2) a weak or missing thesis; (3) paragraphs with no topic sentence; (4) running out of time before the conclusion; and (5) careless errors. A short plan solves the first four; a fixed checking routine solves the fifth.</p>\n<p>The same skills help you answer STEP Composition Analysis questions quickly. Train yourself to recognize each question type in seconds: irrelevant sentence → find the topic; order → look for the first sentence and the linkers; topic or concluding sentence → look at the whole paragraph; transition → decide the relationship; error → find the subject and verb first; paraphrase → check certainty, quantity and cause.</p>\n<p><strong>Examples:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>minute 0–5</strong> Underline: 'Do the ADVANTAGES of REMOTE WORK outweigh the DISADVANTAGES?' → position: yes, with conditions.</p>\n<p><strong>plan</strong> R1 saves time and money · R2 flexibility and productivity · C fewer social connections → solution: hybrid days.</p>\n<p><strong>minute 5–8</strong> Introduction: hook + background + thesis.</p>\n<p><strong>minute 8–29</strong> Three body paragraphs, about 7 minutes each, each starting with a topic sentence.</p>\n<p><strong>minute 29–33</strong> Conclusion: restate the thesis + final thought.</p>\n<p><strong>minute 33–40</strong> Check: agreement → tenses → articles → spelling → punctuation.</p>\n<p><strong>✗ off-topic</strong> Technology has changed the world in many ways. (too general for this question)</p>\n<p><strong>✓ on-topic</strong> For many office workers, remote work offers more benefits than drawbacks.</p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><strong><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">المهارة</span></strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">الكتابة المؤقتة سباق مع الوقت، فاتبع خطة ثابتة لأربعين دقيقة: خمس دقائق لتحليل السؤال والتخطيط، وثمانٍ وعشرون دقيقة للكتابة، وسبع دقائق للمراجعة. وأشهر المشكلات: عدم الإجابة عن السؤال نفسه، وضعف الأطروحة، وغياب جمل الموضوع، ونفاد الوقت قبل الخاتمة، والأخطاء الناتجة عن الاستعجال. والمهارات نفسها تساعدك على التعرف بسرعة على نوع سؤال تحليل الكتابة في STEP وطريقة حله.</span></p>\n<h3>Strategy</h3>\n<blockquote>\n<p>1. Spend the first minutes understanding the exact question; never skip the plan.</p>\n<p>2. Write the thesis and the topic sentences first in your plan; the details can come as you write.</p>\n<p>3. Keep each body paragraph to one main idea with one example.</p>\n<p>4. Leave time for the conclusion: a short conclusion is better than none.</p>\n<p>5. In the exam, identify the question type first, then apply its strategy.</p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">اقضِ الدقائق الأولى في فهم السؤال بدقة ولا تتجاوز التخطيط، واكتب الأطروحة وجمل الموضوع في الخطة أولًا، واجعل لكل فقرة فكرة واحدة ومثالًا واحدًا، واترك وقتًا للخاتمة، وفي الاختبار حدد نوع السؤال أولًا ثم طبّق استراتيجيته.</span></p>\n</blockquote>\n<h3>Traps and Common Mistakes</h3>\n<blockquote>\n<p>✗ Writing about the general topic instead of the exact question.</p>\n<p>✗ Spending too long on the introduction.</p>\n<p>✗ Adding a new argument in the conclusion.</p>\n<p>✗ Skipping the final check because time is short.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<h3>Worked STEP Examples (not counted in the quiz)</h3>\n<p><strong>Example 1. An essay question asks: 'Some companies now allow employees to work from home permanently. Do the advantages outweigh the disadvantages?' Which thesis answers the question most directly?</strong></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>A. Technology has changed the way people live and work.</p>\n<p>B. Many companies have offices in large cities.</p>\n<p>C. For most office workers, the advantages of working from home permanently outweigh the disadvantages, provided that teams still meet regularly.</p>\n<p>D. Working from home became common in 2020.</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> The question asks for a judgement: do the advantages outweigh the disadvantages?</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> The thesis must give that judgement clearly.</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> The other options are background facts that do not answer the question.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>Answer: C</strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">الأطروحة يجب أن تجيب عن السؤال نفسه.</span></p>\n<p><strong>Example 2. Choose the best order for the sentences.</strong></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p><strong>(1)</strong> Then write the body paragraphs, each with a topic sentence and an example.</p>\n<p><strong>(2)</strong> Start by underlining the key words in the question and deciding your position.</p>\n<p><strong>(3)</strong> Finally, spend the last few minutes checking grammar and spelling.</p>\n<p><strong>(4)</strong> Next, write a short introduction that ends with your thesis.</p>\n<p><strong>(5)</strong> After that, write a brief conclusion that restates your thesis.</p>\n<p>A. 2 – 1 – 4 – 5 – 3 B. 2 – 4 – 1 – 5 – 3</p>\n<p>C. 4 – 2 – 1 – 5 – 3 D. 2 – 4 – 1 – 3 – 5</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> The first step is planning (Start by …).</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> Next / Then / After that follow the order of the essay.</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> Finally, checking comes last.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>Answer: B</strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">الكلمات المفتاحية تدل على الترتيب.</span></p>\n<p><strong>Example 3. Remote workers (A) <u>often</u> say that the lack of (B) <u>face-to-face</u> meetings (C) <u>make</u> it harder (D) <u>to build</u> relationships.</strong></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>A. often B. face-to-face C. make D. to build</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> The verb make follows the long phrase 'the lack of face-to-face meetings'.</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> The head noun is lack (singular).</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> A singular subject needs makes.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>Answer: C</strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">ابحث عن الاسم الرئيس في العبارة الطويلة.</span></p>\n<h3>Writing Task W-B2+-04 — Remote work: benefits and drawbacks (timed)</h3>\n<blockquote>\n<p><strong>Task:</strong> Timed task (40 minutes): Some companies now allow employees to work from home permanently. Do the advantages of this outweigh the disadvantages? Write 250–300 words. Spend 5 minutes planning and 7 minutes checking.</p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">مهمة مؤقتة (أربعون دقيقة): تسمح بعض الشركات لموظفيها بالعمل من المنزل بشكل دائم. هل تفوق المزايا العيوب؟ اكتب من مئتين وخمسين إلى ثلاثمئة كلمة، وخصص خمس دقائق للتخطيط وسبع دقائق للمراجعة.</span></p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>Planning frame</strong></p>\n<p>1. Plan (5 min): position, two advantages, one disadvantage + solution.</p>\n<p>2. Introduction (3 min): hook + background + thesis.</p>\n<p>3. Body 1 (7 min): time and money saved.</p>\n<p>4. Body 2 (7 min): flexibility and productivity.</p>\n<p>5. Body 3 (7 min): the disadvantage (isolation) + solution.</p>\n<p>6. Conclusion (3 min) + check (7 min).</p>\n<p><strong>Model answer (250 words; target 250–300)</strong></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>How much of your life do you spend in traffic? For many employees in large cities such as Riyadh, the answer is more than an hour every day. Since 2020, a growing number of companies have allowed staff to work from home permanently. In my opinion, the advantages of this arrangement outweigh the disadvantages, as long as teams still meet regularly.</p>\n<p>The most obvious benefit is the time and money that employees save. Without a daily commute, workers spend less on petrol and have more time for their families, exercise and rest. Companies also save money on office space and electricity.</p>\n<p>Secondly, working from home often increases productivity. Employees can organize their day around the hours when they concentrate best, and there are fewer interruptions from noisy offices and unnecessary meetings. Several studies have found that remote workers complete as much work as their colleagues in the office, and sometimes more.</p>\n<p>Admittedly, remote work has a serious drawback: isolation. Employees may feel lonely, and it can be harder for new staff to learn from experienced colleagues. Communication problems can also slow down teamwork. However, these problems can be reduced if companies organize regular meetings, online or face to face, and encourage teams to stay in daily contact.</p>\n<p>In conclusion, permanent remote work saves time and money and allows employees to work more effectively. Although it can create a sense of isolation, careful planning can solve this problem. For most office workers, home has become a perfectly good place to work.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>Examiner's commentary</strong></p>\n<p>▸ The thesis answers the exact question (Do the advantages outweigh the disadvantages?) and adds a condition.</p>\n<p>▸ Each body paragraph starts with a clear topic sentence (The most obvious benefit … / Secondly … / Admittedly …).</p>\n<p>▸ The counter-argument is conceded and answered with a practical solution.</p>\n<p>▸ The essay is complete within the time: a short but effective conclusion is better than an unfinished body paragraph.</p>\n<p><strong>Self-check before you hand in</strong></p>\n<p>☐ Did I answer the exact question?</p>\n<p>☐ Is my thesis clear in the introduction?</p>\n<p>☐ Does every body paragraph begin with a topic sentence?</p>\n<p>☐ Did I finish with a conclusion?</p>\n<p>☐ Did I check agreement, tenses, articles and spelling?</p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">تأكد من الإجابة عن السؤال نفسه، ووضوح الأطروحة، ووجود جملة موضوع لكل فقرة، وكتابة الخاتمة، ومراجعة الأخطاء.</span></p>","wu":"Worked examples: Example 1 C · Example 2 B · Example 3 C","quiz":[{"l":["Answer all 30 questions. Read each paragraph or sentence carefully and choose the best answer (A, B, C or D).","أجب عن الأسئلة الثلاثين جميعها. اقرأ كل فقرة أو جملة بعناية واختر الإجابة الصحيحة من بين البدائل الأربعة.","Part A — Lesson Focus (Questions 1–20)","الجزء الأول: أسئلة على مهارة الدرس."],"q":[{"n":1,"s":"An essay question asks: 'Should university students be required to do community service?' Which thesis answers the question most directly?","o":["University students should be required to complete community service because it builds responsibility and practical skills.","Community service is common in many countries.","University students study many different subjects.","Volunteering can take place at weekends."],"k":0,"e":"[topic sentence / thesis] University students should be required to complete community service because it builds responsibility and practical skills. — A clear yes, with reasons.","h":"إجابة واضحة مع أسباب."},{"n":2,"s":"Which sentence does NOT belong in the paragraph?","o":["Sentence 3","Sentence 4","Sentence 5","Sentence 6"],"x":["(1) Planning is the most important stage of timed writing. (2) A short plan helps writers stay focused on the question. (3) It also prevents them from repeating the same ideas. (4) Some writers prefer to use blue ink. (5) Even a three-minute plan can improve the organization of an essay. (6) Experienced writers never skip this stage."],"k":1,"e":"[irrelevant sentence] Sentence 4 — The colour of the ink is not about planning.","h":"لون الحبر خارج الموضوع."},{"n":3,"s":"Which word or phrase best fills the blank?","o":["As a result","Nevertheless","In contrast","Otherwise"],"x":["Working from home saves time. ______, it allows employees to spend more time with their families."],"k":0,"e":"[transition / connector] As a result — More family time is a result of saving time.","h":"نتيجة توفير الوقت."},{"n":4,"s":"(A) Many employees (B) who work from home (C) says that they (D) feel more productive.","o":["Many","who","says","feel"],"k":2,"e":"[error] says — The subject employees is plural: say.","h":"الفاعل جمع."},{"n":5,"s":"Which sentence is the best concluding sentence for the paragraph?","o":["Many students write their essays at home.","Repetition is common in long essays.","Planning, therefore, is time well spent rather than time wasted.","Some exams last for three hours."],"x":["Students who plan before they write produce better-organized essays. They stay on topic, avoid repetition and are more likely to finish on time. Even a short plan of three or four lines can make a significant difference. ______"],"k":2,"e":"[concluding sentence] Planning, therefore, is time well spent rather than time wasted. — A conclusion drawn from all the benefits of planning.","h":"خلاصة الفوائد."},{"n":6,"s":"Which sentence is the most appropriate for an academic essay?","o":["Remote work is super good for traffic in big cities.","Remote work kind of fixes the traffic mess.","Remote work totally kills the traffic problem.","Remote work can reduce traffic congestion in major cities."],"k":3,"e":"[word choice / register] Remote work can reduce traffic congestion in major cities. — Formal and precise.","h":"رسمية ودقيقة."},{"n":7,"s":"Choose the best order for the sentences.","o":["2 – 3 – 1 – 4","2 – 1 – 3 – 4","3 – 2 – 1 – 4","2 – 3 – 4 – 1"],"x":["(1) However, some employees find it difficult to separate work from home life.","(2) Many companies now offer flexible working arrangements.","(3) These arrangements help employees balance their professional and family responsibilities.","(4) Clear working hours can help to solve this problem."],"k":0,"e":"[best order] 2 – 3 – 1 – 4 — topic → benefit → However (problem) → solution.","h":"موضوع ثم فائدة ثم مشكلة ثم حل."},{"n":8,"s":"Which sentence best paraphrases: 'Remote workers are less likely to take sick days than office workers.'?","o":["Remote workers are never ill.","Office workers take fewer sick days than remote workers.","Remote workers are more likely to become ill.","Employees who work from home tend to be absent through illness less often than those in offices."],"k":3,"e":"[paraphrase / summary] Employees who work from home tend to be absent through illness less often than those in offices. — less likely to take sick days = absent through illness less often.","h":"المعنى نفسه."},{"n":9,"s":"Which sentence best fills the blank in the paragraph?","o":["Conclusions are usually shorter than introductions.","Some students write very slowly.","To avoid this, they should keep an eye on the clock and stop writing body paragraphs on time.","Essays are marked by experienced teachers."],"x":["Many students run out of time before writing their conclusion. ______ A two-sentence conclusion that restates the thesis is enough to complete the essay."],"k":2,"e":"[complete the paragraph] To avoid this, they should keep an eye on the clock and stop writing body paragraphs on time. — To avoid this answers the problem and leads to the advice.","h":"To avoid this تعالج المشكلة."},{"n":10,"s":"Which topic sentence best fits this body paragraph?","o":["Some employees start work at seven o'clock.","Parents usually take their children to school.","Flexible working hours give employees greater control over their lives.","Companies employ thousands of people."],"x":["______ Employees can start earlier or finish later, and parents can arrange their work around school times. This freedom often makes workers happier and more loyal to their companies."],"k":2,"e":"[topic sentence / thesis] Flexible working hours give employees greater control over their lives. — It introduces the control and freedom explained in the details.","h":"تقدم فكرة التحكم في الوقت."},{"n":11,"s":"If the company (A) had provided better equipment, the employees (B) would work (C) more efficiently (D) last year.","o":["had provided","would work","more","last year"],"k":1,"e":"[error] would work — A past unreal result needs would have worked.","h":"الشرط الثالث: would have worked."},{"n":12,"s":"Which word or phrase best fills the blank?","o":["therefore","for example","similarly","however"],"x":["Some employees enjoy working alone; ______, others miss the social life of the office."],"k":3,"e":"[transition / connector] however — Two contrasting groups.","h":"مجموعتان متقابلتان."},{"n":13,"s":"Which sentence best summarizes this paragraph?","o":["Online meetings always last thirty minutes.","Online meetings are convenient but can be tiring and unreliable, so some companies are keeping them short.","People in different cities never meet face to face.","Technical problems are the main cause of tiredness."],"x":["Online meetings save travel time and allow people in different cities to work together easily. However, many participants find them tiring, and technical problems often interrupt discussions. Some companies now limit online meetings to thirty minutes."],"k":1,"e":"[paraphrase / summary] Online meetings are convenient but can be tiring and unreliable, so some companies are keeping them short. — Benefit + problems + response.","h":"الفائدة والمشكلات والاستجابة."},{"n":14,"s":"Which word best completes the sentence: 'The manager asked the team to ______ their reports by Thursday.'?","o":["submit","hand up","send off up","give out"],"k":0,"e":"[word choice / register] submit — submit = formally hand in.","h":"submit تعني يسلّم رسميًا."},{"n":15,"s":"Which sentence does NOT belong in the paragraph?","o":["Sentence 2","Sentence 3","Sentence 4","Sentence 5"],"x":["(1) Remote work has changed the role of the office. (2) Many companies now use their offices mainly for meetings and teamwork. (3) Some have replaced fixed desks with shared spaces. (4) Others have moved to smaller buildings to save money. (5) Office chairs can be very expensive. (6) The office is becoming a meeting place rather than a place for daily work."],"k":3,"e":"[irrelevant sentence] Sentence 5 — The price of chairs is not about the changing role of the office.","h":"سعر الكراسي خارج الموضوع."},{"n":16,"s":"(A) Not only does remote work save time, (B) but it also (C) reduces stress and (D) improving concentration.","o":["Not only","but","reduces","improving"],"k":3,"e":"[error] improving — Parallel verbs: reduces stress and improves concentration.","h":"التوازي: improves."},{"n":17,"s":"Which sentence best concludes this essay?","o":["With careful planning, the benefits of remote work can be enjoyed while its drawbacks are kept to a minimum.","Isolation is a problem for many elderly people.","Some companies have more than one office.","Productivity is measured in different ways."],"x":["Remote work has clear advantages for employees and companies. It saves time and money and can increase productivity. On the other hand, it may lead to isolation and communication problems. ______"],"k":0,"e":"[concluding sentence] With careful planning, the benefits of remote work can be enjoyed while its drawbacks are kept to a minimum. — A balanced final judgement.","h":"حكم نهائي متوازن."},{"n":18,"s":"Which word or phrase best fills the blank?","o":["Owing to","In spite of","Instead of","Because"],"x":["______ the many benefits of remote work, some employees still prefer to go to the office every day."],"k":1,"e":"[transition / connector] In spite of — In spite of + noun: contrast.","h":"In spite of للتضاد."},{"n":19,"s":"Choose the best order for the sentences.","o":["2 – 3 – 4 – 1","2 – 4 – 3 – 1","4 – 2 – 3 – 1","2 – 4 – 1 – 3"],"x":["(1) Finally, read your essay again to check for errors.","(2) Begin by reading the question carefully.","(3) Then write your essay, following your plan.","(4) Next, make a short plan with your main ideas."],"k":1,"e":"[best order] 2 – 4 – 3 – 1 — Begin → Next → Then → Finally.","h":"ترتيب خطوات الكتابة المؤقتة."},{"n":20,"s":"Which sentence is written correctly?","o":["The number of employees working remotely have doubled since 2019.","The number of employees working remotely has doubled since 2019 year.","The number of employees working remotely has doubled since 2019.","The number of employee working remotely has doubled since 2019."],"k":2,"e":"[error] The number of employees working remotely has doubled since 2019. — The number of + plural noun + singular verb.","h":"The number مع فعل مفرد."}]},{"l":["Part B — Mixed STEP Composition Analysis (Questions 21–30)","الجزء الثاني: أسئلة متنوعة من قسم تحليل الكتابة في اختبار STEP."],"q":[{"n":21,"s":"Which sentence best paraphrases: 'Few candidates finished the essay within the time limit.'?","o":["Most candidates finished the essay on time.","No candidates started the essay.","A few candidates finished the essay early, so the others failed.","Only a small number of candidates completed the essay in the time allowed."],"k":3,"e":"[paraphrase / summary] Only a small number of candidates completed the essay in the time allowed. — Few = only a small number.","h":"Few تعني عددًا قليلًا."},{"n":22,"s":"Which topic sentence best fits this paragraph?","o":["Spelling is difficult in English.","Some exams are marked by computers.","Checking is an essential final step in timed writing.","Writers use many different tenses."],"x":["______ Writers who check their work can find mistakes in agreement, tenses and spelling that would otherwise lower their marks. Even five minutes of checking can make a noticeable difference."],"k":2,"e":"[topic sentence / thesis] Checking is an essential final step in timed writing. — It states the point developed by the details.","h":"تذكر النقطة الرئيسة."},{"n":23,"s":"Which word or phrase best fills the blank?","o":["Nevertheless","Therefore","Likewise","For example"],"x":["The essay was well organized. ______, it contained several grammar mistakes that lowered the final mark."],"k":0,"e":"[transition / connector] Nevertheless — A contrast between organization and accuracy.","h":"تضاد بين التنظيم والدقة."},{"n":24,"s":"By the time the exam (A) ended, most students (B) have (C) written (D) at least three paragraphs.","o":["ended","have","written","at least"],"k":1,"e":"[error] have — The earlier past action needs had written.","h":"الماضي التام."},{"n":25,"s":"Which sentence does NOT belong in the paragraph?","o":["Sentence 1","Sentence 2","Sentence 3","Sentence 4"],"x":["(1) A good conclusion restates the thesis in new words. (2) It may also summarize the main points. (3) Some writers end with a recommendation or a final thought. (4) Introductions often begin with a question. (5) A conclusion should not introduce new arguments."],"k":3,"e":"[irrelevant sentence] Sentence 4 — The sentence about introductions does not belong in a paragraph about conclusions.","h":"الجملة عن المقدمة."},{"n":26,"s":"Which sentence best fills the blank in the paragraph?","o":["Background information can be interesting.","This uses up valuable minutes at the start of the exam.","Introductions are the first paragraph of an essay.","Some candidates write very short essays."],"x":["Many candidates write long introductions with too much background. ______ As a result, they have less time to develop their main arguments."],"k":1,"e":"[complete the paragraph] This uses up valuable minutes at the start of the exam. — This (the long introductions) leads to As a result.","h":"This تعود إلى المقدمات الطويلة."},{"n":27,"s":"Which is the most concise version of 'At this moment in time, the company is currently reviewing its policy.'?","o":["The company is currently reviewing its policy.","At this moment in time, the company is reviewing at present its policy.","Currently, at this moment, the company is now reviewing its policy.","The company, at this moment in time, is currently reviewing its policy."],"k":0,"e":"[word choice / register] The company is currently reviewing its policy. — No repeated time expressions.","h":"دون تكرار."},{"n":28,"s":"Which sentence is the best concluding sentence for the paragraph?","o":["Practising timed writing is therefore an investment in students' future success.","University students write many essays.","Workplaces can be stressful.","Grammar is taught in every school."],"x":["Timed writing tests more than grammar and vocabulary. It shows whether students can think quickly, organize their ideas and express them clearly under pressure. These skills are also needed at university and in the workplace. ______"],"k":0,"e":"[concluding sentence] Practising timed writing is therefore an investment in students' future success. — A conclusion that links the skill to the future.","h":"خلاصة تربط المهارة بالمستقبل."},{"n":29,"s":"Choose the best order for the sentences.","o":["2 – 4 – 3 – 1","3 – 2 – 4 – 1","2 – 3 – 1 – 4","2 – 3 – 4 – 1"],"x":["(1) As a result, she had time to check her essay carefully.","(2) Sara spent five minutes planning her essay.","(3) Her plan helped her write each paragraph quickly.","(4) She finished writing ten minutes before the end of the exam."],"k":3,"e":"[best order] 2 – 3 – 4 – 1 — plan → wrote quickly → finished early → As a result, checked.","h":"تسلسل الأحداث."},{"n":30,"s":"The examiners (A) noticed that essays (B) with a clear plan (C) was usually (D) better organized.","o":["noticed","with","was","better"],"k":2,"e":"[error] was — The subject essays is plural: were.","h":"الفاعل جمع."}]}],"n":30},{"id":"5.5","t":"Integrated Composition Analysis Sets","html":"<p><strong>Unit 5 · Lesson 5.5 · CEFR B2+ · STEP link: Composition Analysis (10%)</strong></p>\n<h3>Objectives</h3>\n<p>1. Answer mixed Composition Analysis questions based on paragraphs from the same essay.</p>\n<p>2. Use the essay's thesis and organization to answer each question faster and more accurately.</p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><strong><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">الأهداف</span></strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">١. أن يجيب الطالب عن أسئلة تحليل كتابة متنوعة مبنية على فقرات من مقال واحد.</span></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">٢. أن يستخدم أطروحة المقال وتنظيمه للإجابة عن كل سؤال بسرعة ودقة أكبر.</span></p>\n<h3>The Skill</h3>\n<p>In an integrated set, several questions come from paragraphs of the SAME essay: one asks for the thesis, another for an irrelevant sentence in a body paragraph, another for the best transition, the order of sentences, an error or the conclusion. The essay's thesis is your map. Once you know the writer's position and plan (for example, 'Saudi Arabia must conserve water through technology, pricing and education'), you can predict what each paragraph should do.</p>\n<p>Ask three questions for every paragraph: WHERE is it in the essay (introduction, body, counter-argument, conclusion)? WHAT is its job (present a reason, give evidence, answer an objection, sum up)? HOW does it connect to the thesis? A sentence that does not serve the paragraph's job is irrelevant; a topic sentence must match the paragraph's job; a conclusion must match the thesis; a transition must match the relationship between this paragraph and the one before.</p>\n<p>Integrated sets also test consistency across the essay. The same term should be used in the same way (do not switch from 'water conservation' to 'water production'); the tone should stay formal; the position should not change; and examples should support the paragraph in which they appear. Keep the whole essay in mind, not only the sentence in front of you.</p>\n<p><strong>Examples:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>thesis (map)</strong> Saudi Arabia must conserve water through technology, fair pricing and public education.</p>\n<p><strong>Body 1 job</strong> technology → smart irrigation, leak detection, recycled water</p>\n<p><strong>Body 2 job</strong> fair pricing → paying for what you use encourages saving</p>\n<p><strong>Body 3 job</strong> education → schools and media campaigns change habits</p>\n<p><strong>counter-argument</strong> Critics say higher prices hurt poor families. → However, a basic allowance can be kept cheap.</p>\n<p><strong>✗ irrelevant</strong> In Body 2: 'Many people enjoy swimming in the summer.'</p>\n<p><strong>✗ inconsistent</strong> Thesis about saving water; conclusion about building more desalination plants only.</p>\n<p><strong>✓ consistent conclusion</strong> Only by combining technology, pricing and education can the Kingdom secure its water future.</p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><strong><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">المهارة</span></strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">في الأسئلة المتكاملة تأتي عدة أسئلة من فقرات مقال واحد، والأطروحة هي خريطتك: إذا عرفت موقف الكاتب وخطته تستطيع توقع وظيفة كل فقرة. واسأل لكل فقرة: أين موقعها؟ وما وظيفتها؟ وكيف ترتبط بالأطروحة؟ كما تختبر هذه الأسئلة الاتساق في المصطلحات والأسلوب والموقف والأمثلة عبر المقال كله.</span></p>\n<h3>Strategy</h3>\n<blockquote>\n<p>1. Find or predict the thesis first; it tells you the plan of the essay.</p>\n<p>2. Label each paragraph with its job before answering its question.</p>\n<p>3. Check every answer against both the paragraph AND the thesis.</p>\n<p>4. Watch for inconsistency: a change of term, tone or position.</p>\n<p>5. Use what you learned in earlier questions of the set to answer later ones.</p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">حدد الأطروحة أو توقعها أولًا، وسمِّ وظيفة كل فقرة قبل الإجابة عن سؤالها، وطابق كل إجابة مع الفقرة ومع الأطروحة، وانتبه لتغيّر المصطلح أو الأسلوب أو الموقف، واستفد من الأسئلة السابقة في الإجابة عن اللاحقة.</span></p>\n</blockquote>\n<h3>Traps and Common Mistakes</h3>\n<blockquote>\n<p>✗ Choosing an answer that fits the sentence but not the essay's thesis.</p>\n<p>✗ Accepting a conclusion that changes the writer's position.</p>\n<p>✗ Ignoring the paragraph's job (for example, a counter-argument paragraph).</p>\n<p>✗ Missing a change of key term or tone.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<h3>Worked STEP Examples (not counted in the quiz)</h3>\n<p><strong>Example 1. Which sentence is the best thesis statement for this introduction?</strong></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Saudi Arabia is one of the driest countries in the world, yet its citizens use more water per person than people in most other countries. Groundwater is running low, and desalination is expensive and energy-intensive. ______</p>\n<p>A. Desalination plants are built along the coast.</p>\n<p>B. To secure its water future, the Kingdom must reduce consumption through technology, fair pricing and public education.</p>\n<p>C. Water is essential for all living things.</p>\n<p>D. Many countries have rivers and lakes.</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> The introduction presents a problem: high use, low supply.</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> The thesis should give the writer's position and plan.</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> Only the correct answer offers a position with three previewed points.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>Answer: B</strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">الأطروحة تقدم الموقف وخطة المقال.</span></p>\n<p><strong>Example 2. Which word or phrase best fills the blank?</strong></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>[Body 2] ______, water pricing can encourage people to save. When households pay according to how much they use, they quickly fix leaks and avoid waste.</p>\n<p>A. Instead of saving water B. Unlike fair pricing</p>\n<p>C. Because of low prices D. In addition to new technology</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> The thesis lists technology, pricing, education.</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> Body 2 is about pricing, so it adds a second solution.</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> In addition to new technology links Body 1 and Body 2.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>Answer: D</strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">الأداة تربط الفقرة بما قبلها حسب خطة الأطروحة.</span></p>\n<p><strong>Example 3. Which sentence best concludes the essay?</strong></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>[Conclusion] Water is the Kingdom's most precious resource. Smart technology can reduce losses, fair prices can change habits, and education can create a generation that values every drop. ______</p>\n<p>A. Only by combining these three approaches can Saudi Arabia secure its water supply for future generations.</p>\n<p>B. Desalination is the best solution to the water problem.</p>\n<p>C. Many people drink bottled water.</p>\n<p>D. Rain is rare in most parts of the country.</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> The conclusion repeats the three solutions.</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> The final sentence must restate the thesis.</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> One distractor changes the position; the other two are neutral facts.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>Answer: A</strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">الخاتمة يجب أن تتسق مع الأطروحة.</span></p>\n<h3>Writing Task W-B2+-05 — Water conservation in dry countries</h3>\n<blockquote>\n<p><strong>Task:</strong> Write an essay of 250–300 words: 'How can Saudi Arabia conserve water?' Give a clear thesis that previews your solutions, develop each solution in its own paragraph, include one counter-argument and keep your terms and position consistent to the end.</p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">اكتب مقالًا من مئتين وخمسين إلى ثلاثمئة كلمة: كيف يمكن للمملكة العربية السعودية أن تحافظ على المياه؟ اكتب أطروحة واضحة تعرض حلولك، وطوّر كل حل في فقرة مستقلة، وأضف رأيًا مقابلًا، وحافظ على اتساق المصطلحات والموقف حتى النهاية.</span></p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>Planning frame</strong></p>\n<p>1. Introduction: hook + problem + thesis with three solutions.</p>\n<p>2. Body 1: technology.</p>\n<p>3. Body 2: fair pricing + counter-argument and rebuttal.</p>\n<p>4. Body 3: education.</p>\n<p>5. Conclusion: restate the thesis + final thought.</p>\n<p><strong>Model answer (254 words; target 250–300)</strong></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Saudi Arabia has no permanent rivers, yet its people use more water per person than people in most countries. Groundwater that took thousands of years to collect is being used up, and desalination requires huge amounts of energy. To secure its water future, the Kingdom must reduce consumption through technology, fair pricing and public education.</p>\n<p>Firstly, technology can prevent a great deal of waste. Smart irrigation systems give crops only the water they need, while sensors can detect leaks in city pipes before they become serious. Treated waste water can also be reused to water parks and trees instead of fresh drinking water.</p>\n<p>In addition to new technology, fair pricing can encourage people to save. When households pay according to how much they use, they quickly fix leaks and avoid waste. Critics argue that higher prices would hurt low-income families. However, the government can keep a basic monthly allowance cheap and charge more only for heavy use.</p>\n<p>Finally, education is essential, because habits are formed early. Schools can teach children to turn off taps, take shorter showers and report leaks, and media campaigns can remind adults that every drop matters. Such efforts have already changed attitudes in many Saudi homes, and they cost far less than building new plants.</p>\n<p>In conclusion, water is the Kingdom's most precious resource. Smart technology can reduce losses, fair prices can change habits, and education can create a generation that values every drop. Only by combining these three approaches can Saudi Arabia secure its water supply for future generations.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>Examiner's commentary</strong></p>\n<p>▸ The thesis previews three solutions, and the body paragraphs keep that order.</p>\n<p>▸ Transitions (Firstly / In addition to new technology / Finally) show the plan clearly.</p>\n<p>▸ The counter-argument is placed in the paragraph it belongs to (pricing) and answered with a practical solution.</p>\n<p>▸ Key terms and the writer's position stay consistent; the conclusion mirrors the thesis.</p>\n<p><strong>Self-check before you hand in</strong></p>\n<p>☐ Does my thesis preview my solutions?</p>\n<p>☐ Does each body paragraph develop one solution in the same order?</p>\n<p>☐ Did I include and answer a counter-argument?</p>\n<p>☐ Are my terms, tone and position consistent?</p>\n<p>☐ Is my essay 250–300 words?</p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">تأكد من أن الأطروحة تعرض الحلول، وأن الفقرات تتبع ترتيبها، وأنك أجبت عن الرأي المقابل، وحافظت على الاتساق.</span></p>","wu":"Worked examples: Example 1 B · Example 2 D · Example 3 A","quiz":[{"l":["Answer all 30 questions. Read each paragraph or sentence carefully and choose the best answer (A, B, C or D).","أجب عن الأسئلة الثلاثين جميعها. اقرأ كل فقرة أو جملة بعناية واختر الإجابة الصحيحة من بين البدائل الأربعة.","Part A — Lesson Focus (Questions 1–20)","الجزء الأول: أسئلة على مهارة الدرس."],"q":[{"n":1,"s":"Which sentence is the best thesis statement for this introduction?","o":["Makkah and Madinah are holy cities.","Many visitors travel from Asia and Africa.","Smart technology, improved transport and well-trained staff are the keys to managing these crowds safely.","Vision 2030 was announced in 2016."],"x":["Every year, millions of visitors come to Makkah and Madinah, and the number is expected to grow under Vision 2030. Managing such huge crowds safely requires careful planning. ______"],"k":2,"e":"[topic sentence / thesis] Smart technology, improved transport and well-trained staff are the keys to managing these crowds safely. — A clear position with three previewed points.","h":"موقف مع ثلاث نقاط."},{"n":2,"s":"Which sentence does NOT belong in the paragraph?","o":["Sentence 2","Sentence 3","Sentence 4","Sentence 5"],"x":["(1) [Body 1] Smart technology is already transforming crowd management. (2) Cameras and sensors track the movement of people in real time. (3) Mobile apps guide visitors along less crowded routes. (4) Some visitors buy dates and perfume as gifts. (5) Control centres can redirect crowds before dangerous situations develop."],"k":2,"e":"[irrelevant sentence] Sentence 4 — Buying gifts is not about crowd-management technology.","h":"شراء الهدايا خارج الموضوع."},{"n":3,"s":"Which word or phrase best fills the blank?","o":["Alongside","Instead of","Despite","Unlike"],"x":["[Body 2] ______ technology, transport plays a vital role. The Haramain High-Speed Railway now carries passengers between Makkah and Madinah in about two hours."],"k":0,"e":"[transition / connector] Alongside — Transport is a second solution added to technology.","h":"حل إضافي."},{"n":4,"s":"(Body 3) The staff (A) who manage the crowds (B) needs (C) special training in safety and (D) communication.","o":["who","needs","special","communication"],"k":1,"e":"[error] needs — The subject staff (the people) takes a plural verb here: need.","h":"staff بمعنى الأشخاص جمع."},{"n":5,"s":"Which sentence best concludes the essay?","o":["Together, these three elements can make every visit both safe and spiritually rewarding.","Some visitors stay for only one day.","The railway was opened in 2018.","Many countries face traffic problems."],"x":["[Conclusion] Managing millions of visitors is one of the greatest challenges any country faces. Technology provides information, transport moves people efficiently, and trained staff make the right decisions on the ground. ______"],"k":0,"e":"[concluding sentence] Together, these three elements can make every visit both safe and spiritually rewarding. — It restates the thesis (three keys) and ends with a final thought.","h":"تعيد الأطروحة بفكرة ختامية."},{"n":6,"s":"Which sentence is the best thesis statement for this introduction?","o":["Cafés are popular in Saudi cities.","Young entrepreneurs succeed most often when they combine careful planning, mentoring and a willingness to learn from failure.","Technology companies employ many people.","Loans must be repaid with interest."],"x":["Many young Saudis are starting their own businesses, from cafés to technology companies. Government programmes offer training and loans, but many start-ups still fail in their first years. ______"],"k":1,"e":"[topic sentence / thesis] Young entrepreneurs succeed most often when they combine careful planning, mentoring and a willingness to learn from failure. — A clear position previewing three points.","h":"موقف مع ثلاث نقاط."},{"n":7,"s":"Choose the best order for the sentences.","o":["2 – 4 – 3 – 1","3 – 2 – 4 – 1","2 – 3 – 4 – 1","2 – 3 – 1 – 4"],"x":["(1) As a result, they avoid running out of money in the first year.","(2) Successful entrepreneurs plan carefully before they start.","(3) They study the market and calculate their costs.","(4) They also prepare for unexpected problems."],"k":2,"e":"[best order] 2 – 3 – 4 – 1 — topic → details → also → As a result.","h":"موضوع ثم تفاصيل ثم نتيجة."},{"n":8,"s":"Which sentence best fills the blank in the paragraph?","o":["Many cafés open late at night.","Experienced business owners can share knowledge that no textbook provides.","Suppliers deliver goods every week.","Some beginners prefer to work alone."],"x":["[Body 2] Mentoring is the second key to success. ______ For instance, an experienced café owner can warn a beginner about common mistakes with suppliers and staff."],"k":1,"e":"[complete the paragraph] Experienced business owners can share knowledge that no textbook provides. — For instance needs a general statement about mentoring first.","h":"For instance تحتاج قبلها فكرة عامة."},{"n":9,"s":"Which word or phrase best fills the blank?","o":["In reality","Similarly","As a result","For this reason"],"x":["[Body 3] Some people believe that failure is the end of a business journey. ______, many successful entrepreneurs failed several times before they found the right idea."],"k":0,"e":"[transition / connector] In reality — In reality rebuts the belief.","h":"In reality للرد."},{"n":10,"s":"(Conclusion) Planning, mentoring and (A) learning from failure (B) are the three (C) keys to (D) succeed.","o":["learning","are","keys","succeed"],"k":3,"e":"[error] succeed — to here is a preposition (the keys to …), so a noun is needed: success.","h":"to حرف جر: success."},{"n":11,"s":"Which sentence does NOT belong in the paragraph?","o":["Sentence 2","Sentence 3","Sentence 4","Sentence 5"],"x":["(1) [Body 1] Public libraries are changing to meet the needs of the digital age. (2) Many now offer free Wi-Fi and computers. (3) Some lend e-books and audiobooks through mobile apps. (4) Others run workshops on coding and digital skills. (5) Printed newspapers were first published in the seventeenth century."],"k":3,"e":"[irrelevant sentence] Sentence 5 — The history of newspapers does not describe how libraries are changing.","h":"تاريخ الصحف خارج الموضوع."},{"n":12,"s":"In an essay about public libraries, which sentence keeps a consistent formal tone?","o":["Libraries also provide quiet spaces where students can study without distraction.","Libraries are also, like, really chill places to study.","Libraries are awesome spots for students to hang out and study.","Libraries are cool for studying, honestly."],"k":0,"e":"[word choice / register] Libraries also provide quiet spaces where students can study without distraction. — Formal tone throughout the essay.","h":"أسلوب رسمي متسق."},{"n":13,"s":"Which topic sentence best fits this body paragraph?","o":["Retired teachers often have free time.","Reading clubs meet at the weekend.","Libraries have also become important community centres.","Artists sell their work in galleries."],"x":["[Body 2] ______ Retired teachers volunteer to help children with homework, families attend weekend reading clubs, and local artists display their work in library halls."],"k":2,"e":"[topic sentence / thesis] Libraries have also become important community centres. — It introduces the three community examples.","h":"تقدم أمثلة المجتمع."},{"n":14,"s":"Which sentence best summarizes this paragraph?","o":["Although some think libraries are unnecessary in the internet age, they still provide free access and reliable information.","Everything is available online today.","Fast internet is expensive in all countries.","Libraries sell devices to families."],"x":["[Body 3] Critics argue that libraries are no longer necessary because everything is available online. However, not every family can afford fast internet or devices, and online information is not always reliable. Libraries offer free access and help users find trustworthy sources."],"k":0,"e":"[paraphrase / summary] Although some think libraries are unnecessary in the internet age, they still provide free access and reliable information. — The objection and the rebuttal in brief.","h":"الاعتراض والرد باختصار."},{"n":15,"s":"Which sentence best concludes the essay?","o":["Some libraries close on Fridays.","Far from disappearing, libraries are more relevant today than ever before.","Books are heavy to carry.","Many people read on their phones."],"x":["[Conclusion] Public libraries have adapted to the digital age by offering technology, community activities and reliable information. They serve people of every age and income. ______"],"k":1,"e":"[concluding sentence] Far from disappearing, libraries are more relevant today than ever before. — A final statement consistent with the thesis.","h":"عبارة ختامية متسقة."},{"n":16,"s":"Libraries (A) that offer digital services (B) attract (C) much more young people than those (D) who do not.","o":["that","attract","much","who"],"k":3,"e":"[error] who — those refers to libraries (things): those that do not.","h":"those تعود إلى أشياء: that."},{"n":17,"s":"Which word or phrase best fills the blank?","o":["At the same time","For example","As a result","In other words"],"x":["[Body 1] Online learning has expanded rapidly. ______, it has created new problems, such as screen fatigue and a lack of social interaction."],"k":0,"e":"[transition / connector] At the same time — At the same time introduces a contrasting side effect.","h":"تقديم جانب مقابل."},{"n":18,"s":"Choose the best order for the sentences.","o":["2 – 4 – 3 – 1","3 – 2 – 4 – 1","2 – 1 – 3 – 4","2 – 3 – 4 – 1"],"x":["(1) Despite these problems, online learning is here to stay.","(2) Online learning offers flexibility and access to world-class courses.","(3) However, some students struggle with motivation when studying alone.","(4) Others lack reliable internet at home."],"k":3,"e":"[best order] 2 – 3 – 4 – 1 — benefit → However (problem) → Others (problem 2) → Despite these problems (conclusion).","h":"فائدة ثم مشكلتان ثم خلاصة."},{"n":19,"s":"Which sentence best fills the blank in the paragraph?","o":["Laptops are expensive in some countries.","They can provide regular video meetings with teachers to keep students motivated.","Some teachers prefer printed books.","Video meetings were rare in the past."],"x":["[Body 2] Schools can support online learners in several ways. ______ They can also lend laptops to students who do not have their own."],"k":1,"e":"[complete the paragraph] They can provide regular video meetings with teachers to keep students motivated. — also needs a first way of supporting learners before it.","h":"also تحتاج طريقة أولى قبلها."},{"n":20,"s":"Which sentence keeps the key term consistent in an essay about 'online learning'?","o":["Online shopping allows students to study at their own pace.","Online gaming allows students to study at their own pace.","Online learning allows students to study at their own pace.","Online banking allows students to study at their own pace."],"k":2,"e":"[error] Online learning allows students to study at their own pace. — The essay's key term must stay the same.","h":"المصطلح الرئيس ثابت."}]},{"l":["Part B — Mixed STEP Composition Analysis (Questions 21–30)","الجزء الثاني: أسئلة متنوعة من قسم تحليل الكتابة في اختبار STEP."],"q":[{"n":21,"s":"Which sentence is the best thesis statement for this introduction?","o":["Heritage tourism can benefit the Kingdom, but only if sites are protected, local communities are involved and visitors are educated.","Hegra is located near AlUla.","Archaeologists study ancient sites.","Many tourists take photographs."],"x":["Saudi Arabia has some of the richest archaeological sites in the region, from Hegra to Diriyah. In the past, few people visited them. Today, they are becoming major tourist attractions. ______"],"k":0,"e":"[topic sentence / thesis] Heritage tourism can benefit the Kingdom, but only if sites are protected, local communities are involved and visitors are educated. — A clear, conditional position with three previewed points.","h":"موقف مشروط بثلاث نقاط."},{"n":22,"s":"Which sentence does NOT belong in the paragraph?","o":["Sentence 1","Sentence 2","Sentence 3","Sentence 4"],"x":["(1) [Body 1] Protecting heritage sites is the first priority. (2) Visitor numbers must be controlled to prevent damage. (3) Paths and platforms keep people away from fragile structures. (4) Many tourists prefer to travel in winter. (5) Regular monitoring helps experts repair problems early."],"k":3,"e":"[irrelevant sentence] Sentence 4 — The travel season is not about protection.","h":"موسم السفر خارج الموضوع."},{"n":23,"s":"Which word or phrase best fills the blank?","o":["Instead of","Besides","Rather than","Unlike"],"x":["[Body 2] ______ protecting the sites, tourism projects must involve local communities."],"k":1,"e":"[transition / connector] Besides — A second requirement is added.","h":"إضافة شرط ثانٍ."},{"n":24,"s":"Local guides, (A) whose families (B) have lived in the area for generations, (C) shares stories that (D) no book contains.","o":["whose","have","shares","no"],"k":2,"e":"[error] shares — The subject Local guides is plural: share.","h":"الفاعل جمع."},{"n":25,"s":"Which sentence best fills the blank in the paragraph?","o":["Visitors often buy souvenirs.","Information centres and guided tours explain the history and importance of each site.","Some sites are open at night.","Tickets can be booked online."],"x":["[Body 3] Visitors also need to understand the value of what they see. ______ As a result, they are more likely to respect the site and follow the rules."],"k":1,"e":"[complete the paragraph] Information centres and guided tours explain the history and importance of each site. — As a result needs a cause: education of visitors.","h":"As a result تحتاج سببًا."},{"n":26,"s":"Which sentence is the best concluding sentence for the paragraph?","o":["Ancient sites are very old.","Jobs are important for young people.","If these conditions are met, the Kingdom's ancient sites can inspire visitors for centuries to come.","International tourists need visas."],"x":["[Conclusion] Heritage tourism offers jobs, pride and international recognition. However, these benefits depend on protection, community involvement and education. ______"],"k":2,"e":"[concluding sentence] If these conditions are met, the Kingdom's ancient sites can inspire visitors for centuries to come. — A final thought consistent with the conditional thesis.","h":"فكرة ختامية متسقة."},{"n":27,"s":"Which sentence best paraphrases: 'Tourism can only be sustainable if local people benefit from it.'?","o":["Local people always benefit from tourism.","Tourism is never sustainable.","Local people make tourism unsustainable.","Unless local communities gain from tourism, it cannot continue successfully in the long term."],"k":3,"e":"[paraphrase / summary] Unless local communities gain from tourism, it cannot continue successfully in the long term. — only … if = unless … not.","h":"only if تعني unless."},{"n":28,"s":"Choose the best order for the sentences.","o":["2 – 1 – 3 – 4","2 – 3 – 1 – 4","3 – 2 – 1 – 4","2 – 3 – 4 – 1"],"x":["(1) This helps them earn money while protecting their traditions.","(2) Many villages near AlUla now welcome tourists.","(3) Residents run guesthouses, restaurants and craft workshops.","(4) Such projects show how tourism can support communities."],"k":1,"e":"[best order] 2 – 3 – 1 – 4 — topic → activities → This (benefit) → Such projects (summary).","h":"موضوع ثم أنشطة ثم فائدة ثم خلاصة."},{"n":29,"s":"Which word best completes the formal sentence: 'The new regulations are designed to ______ the ancient tombs from damage.'?","o":["look after up","keep off","hold up","safeguard"],"k":3,"e":"[word choice / register] safeguard — safeguard = protect (formal).","h":"safeguard تعني يحمي."},{"n":30,"s":"(A) Hardly had the site (B) opened to the public (C) than thousands of visitors (D) arrived.","o":["Hardly","opened","than","arrived"],"k":2,"e":"[error] than — Hardly had … is followed by when, not than.","h":"Hardly … when."}]}],"n":30},{"id":"5.6","t":"Full STEP Composition Analysis Practice","html":"<p><strong>Unit 5 · Lesson 5.6 · CEFR B2+ · STEP link: Composition Analysis (10%)</strong></p>\n<h3>Objectives</h3>\n<p>1. Answer a full set of STEP Composition Analysis questions under exam conditions.</p>\n<p>2. Write a timed STEP-style essay of 250–300 words that is organized, cohesive and accurate.</p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><strong><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">الأهداف</span></strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">١. أن يجيب الطالب عن مجموعة كاملة من أسئلة تحليل الكتابة في STEP تحت ظروف الاختبار.</span></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">٢. أن يكتب مقالًا مؤقتًا بأسلوب STEP من مئتين وخمسين إلى ثلاثمئة كلمة منظمًا ومترابطًا ودقيقًا.</span></p>\n<h3>The Skill</h3>\n<p>Composition Analysis is about 10% of the STEP test, and its questions are mixed. You will not be told which skill each question tests, so the first step is always to RECOGNIZE the type: Which sentence does not belong? (irrelevant sentence); What is the best order? (sentence order); Which sentence best begins / ends the paragraph? (topic / concluding sentence); a gap between ideas (transition or complete the paragraph); four underlined parts (error); Which sentence has the same meaning? (paraphrase); Which word is most appropriate? (word choice).</p>\n<p>Pace yourself. Most Composition Analysis questions should take less than a minute. Answer the quick types first in your mind (transition, error, word choice), and do not let one long ordering question steal time from five others. If you are unsure, ELIMINATE: cross out options that are off-topic, informal, ungrammatical or illogical, then choose between the remaining options by checking the relationship with the sentences before and after.</p>\n<p>At the end, review. Check that you have not changed a correct answer without a clear reason, that you have answered every question (there is no penalty for guessing), and that your answers match the paragraph AND the overall topic. The habits you built in Units 1–5 (finding the topic, following the linkers, checking agreement, testing meaning) are now your exam toolkit.</p>\n<p><strong>Examples:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>irrelevant sentence</strong> Find the topic → test each sentence → remove the one that changes the focus.</p>\n<p><strong>sentence order</strong> Find the opener → follow reference words and linkers → check the final sentence.</p>\n<p><strong>topic sentence</strong> Read all the details → choose the sentence that covers all of them.</p>\n<p><strong>concluding sentence</strong> Restate the main idea → no new facts or new topics.</p>\n<p><strong>transition</strong> Decide the relationship: addition, contrast, cause, result, example, concession.</p>\n<p><strong>error</strong> Subject ↔︎ verb → tense → parallelism → preposition → word form.</p>\n<p><strong>paraphrase</strong> Check certainty, quantity, cause and contrast.</p>\n<p><strong>word choice</strong> Formal, precise and concise.</p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><strong><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">المهارة</span></strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">يشكل تحليل الكتابة نحو عشرة في المئة من اختبار STEP وأسئلته مختلطة، فالخطوة الأولى دائمًا هي التعرف على نوع السؤال. نظّم وقتك بحيث لا يتجاوز معظم الأسئلة دقيقة واحدة، واستخدم الحذف عند الشك، وراجع إجاباتك في النهاية دون تغيير إجابة صحيحة بلا سبب واضح، وأجب عن كل الأسئلة. والعادات التي بنيتها في الوحدات من الأولى إلى الخامسة هي أدواتك في الاختبار.</span></p>\n<h3>Strategy</h3>\n<blockquote>\n<p>1. Recognize the question type in the first few seconds.</p>\n<p>2. Apply that type's routine (topic → linkers → agreement → meaning).</p>\n<p>3. Eliminate clearly wrong options first.</p>\n<p>4. Do not spend more than about a minute on one question; mark it and return.</p>\n<p>5. Answer every question; review only when you have a clear reason to change.</p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">تعرّف على نوع السؤال في الثواني الأولى، وطبّق خطوات حله، واحذف البدائل الخاطئة بوضوح أولًا، ولا تقضِ أكثر من دقيقة تقريبًا في سؤال واحد، وأجب عن كل الأسئلة ولا تغيّر إجابة إلا لسبب واضح.</span></p>\n</blockquote>\n<h3>Traps and Common Mistakes</h3>\n<blockquote>\n<p>✗ Spending too long on one ordering question.</p>\n<p>✗ Choosing an option that is true but does not fit the paragraph.</p>\n<p>✗ Changing a correct answer without a clear reason.</p>\n<p>✗ Leaving questions unanswered.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<h3>Worked STEP Examples (not counted in the quiz)</h3>\n<p><strong>Example 1. Which sentence does NOT belong in the paragraph?</strong></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p><strong>(1)</strong> E-books have changed the way many people read. <strong>(2)</strong> They are light, portable and often cheaper than printed books. <strong>(3)</strong> Readers can carry hundreds of titles on a single device. <strong>(4)</strong> Some e-readers allow users to adjust the size of the text. <strong>(5)</strong> Paper was invented in China about two thousand years ago. <strong>(6)</strong> However, many readers still prefer the feel of a printed book.</p>\n<p>A. Sentence 2 B. Sentence 3 C. Sentence 4 D. Sentence 5</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> Type: Which sentence does not belong? → irrelevant sentence.</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> Topic: how e-books have changed reading (advantages, then However).</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> Sentence 5 jumps to the ancient history of paper.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>Answer: D</strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">تعرّف على النوع ثم طبّق خطواته.</span></p>\n<p><strong>Example 2. Which sentence best paraphrases: 'Sales of printed books have remained surprisingly stable despite the rise of e-books.'?</strong></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>A. Although e-books have become more popular, printed book sales have not changed much, which is unexpected.</p>\n<p>B. Printed book sales have fallen sharply because of e-books.</p>\n<p>C. E-books have become less popular than printed books.</p>\n<p>D. The rise of e-books was caused by stable sales of printed books.</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> Type: same meaning → paraphrase.</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> Key parts: stable sales, surprisingly, despite the rise of e-books.</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> Only the correct answer keeps all three; the distractors change the direction or the cause.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>Answer: A</strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">طابق عناصر المعنى.</span></p>\n<p><strong>Example 3. (A) <u>Although</u> many young people (B) <u>read</u> on screens, (C) <u>but</u> printed books (D) <u>remain</u> popular.</strong></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>A. Although B. read C. but D. remain</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> Type: four underlined parts → error.</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> Although already shows contrast.</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> Adding but creates a double connector, so C is wrong.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>Answer: C</strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">أداة ربط واحدة تكفي.</span></p>\n<h3>Writing Task W-B2+-06 — The value of printed books in a digital age (timed STEP-style essay)</h3>\n<blockquote>\n<p><strong>Task:</strong> Timed STEP-style task (40 minutes): 'In a digital age, printed books will soon disappear.' To what extent do you agree or disagree? Write 250–300 words with a clear thesis, well-organized body paragraphs, a counter-argument and a conclusion.</p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">مهمة مؤقتة بأسلوب STEP (أربعون دقيقة): في العصر الرقمي ستختفي الكتب المطبوعة قريبًا. إلى أي حد توافق أو تخالف؟ اكتب من مئتين وخمسين إلى ثلاثمئة كلمة بأطروحة واضحة وفقرات منظمة ورأي مقابل وخاتمة.</span></p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>Planning frame</strong></p>\n<p>1. Introduction: hook + background + thesis (disagree: books will change, not disappear).</p>\n<p>2. Body 1: the case for e-books (concession).</p>\n<p>3. Body 2: why printed books survive (experience, focus, ownership).</p>\n<p>4. Body 3: evidence (sales, book fairs, children's books).</p>\n<p>5. Conclusion: restate + final thought.</p>\n<p><strong>Model answer (256 words; target 250–300)</strong></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Twenty years ago, many experts predicted that the e-book would soon replace the printed book, just as digital music replaced the cassette. Today, however, bookshops across the world are still open and book fairs are still crowded. I therefore disagree with the statement: printed books will change, but they will not disappear.</p>\n<p>Admittedly, digital reading has clear advantages. E-books are cheap, light and instantly available, and a single device can hold an entire library. For students and frequent travellers, these benefits are difficult to ignore.</p>\n<p>Nevertheless, printed books offer an experience that screens cannot fully copy. Many readers enjoy the feel and smell of paper, and they find it easier to concentrate without notifications interrupting them. Research also suggests that readers often remember more of what they read on paper. In addition, a printed book is something people can own, lend, sign and keep for a lifetime, or even pass on to their children.</p>\n<p>The evidence supports this view. Sales of printed books have remained surprisingly stable in many countries, and events such as the Riyadh International Book Fair attract hundreds of thousands of visitors every year. Parents, in particular, continue to buy picture books for their children, because reading together from a real book is a special family experience.</p>\n<p>In conclusion, digital and printed books are likely to exist side by side. E-books will continue to grow because they are practical, but printed books will survive because they are personal. Rather than disappearing, the printed book is simply finding its place in a digital world.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>Examiner's commentary</strong></p>\n<p>▸ The thesis takes a clear position on the exact statement (disagree) and explains it (change, not disappear).</p>\n<p>▸ The counter-argument is placed first and conceded (Admittedly …), then answered (Nevertheless …).</p>\n<p>▸ Each body paragraph has one job: concession, reasons, evidence.</p>\n<p>▸ The conclusion restates the position with a balanced contrast (practical / personal) and a memorable final sentence.</p>\n<p><strong>Self-check before you hand in</strong></p>\n<p>☐ Did I respond to the exact statement (to what extent)?</p>\n<p>☐ Is my position clear and consistent?</p>\n<p>☐ Did I include and answer a counter-argument?</p>\n<p>☐ Do my paragraphs have clear topic sentences and linkers?</p>\n<p>☐ Did I check agreement, tenses and punctuation, and is my essay 250–300 words?</p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">تأكد من الرد على العبارة نفسها، ووضوح موقفك واتساقه، والرد على الرأي المقابل، ووضوح جمل الموضوع وأدوات الربط، ومراجعة الأخطاء.</span></p>","wu":"Worked examples: Example 1 D · Example 2 A · Example 3 C","quiz":[{"l":["Answer all 30 questions. Read each paragraph or sentence carefully and choose the best answer (A, B, C or D).","أجب عن الأسئلة الثلاثين جميعها. اقرأ كل فقرة أو جملة بعناية واختر الإجابة الصحيحة من بين البدائل الأربعة.","Part A — Lesson Focus (Questions 1–20)","الجزء الأول: أسئلة على مهارة الدرس."],"q":[{"n":1,"s":"Which topic sentence best fits this paragraph?","o":["Interest in printed books is growing among young Saudis.","Social media is popular with teenagers.","Bookshops are open in the evenings.","Screens can cause eye strain."],"x":["______ Bookshops in Riyadh and Jeddah report growing numbers of young customers, and book clubs have become popular on social media. Many teenagers say they enjoy taking a break from screens."],"k":0,"e":"[topic sentence / thesis] Interest in printed books is growing among young Saudis. — It covers all three details about young readers.","h":"تغطي التفاصيل الثلاث."},{"n":2,"s":"Which word or phrase best fills the blank?","o":["As a result","On the other hand","In addition","For instance"],"x":["E-books are convenient. ______, many readers find it harder to concentrate when reading on a screen."],"k":1,"e":"[transition / connector] On the other hand — A contrasting disadvantage.","h":"عيب مقابل."},{"n":3,"s":"The library (A) has (B) introduced a system (C) that (D) allow students to borrow e-books.","o":["has","introduced","that","allow"],"k":3,"e":"[error] allow — that refers to a system (singular): allows.","h":"a system مفرد: allows."},{"n":4,"s":"Which sentence does NOT belong in the paragraph?","o":["Sentence 2","Sentence 3","Sentence 4","Sentence 5"],"x":["(1) Book fairs play an important role in promoting reading. (2) They bring together publishers, authors and readers. (3) Visitors can attend talks and meet their favourite writers. (4) Children's sections encourage young readers to discover new stories. (5) Some exhibition centres also host car shows."],"k":3,"e":"[irrelevant sentence] Sentence 5 — Car shows are not about promoting reading.","h":"معارض السيارات خارج الموضوع."},{"n":5,"s":"Which sentence best paraphrases: 'Students who read for pleasure tend to achieve higher grades in all subjects.'?","o":["Students with high grades never read for pleasure.","Learners who enjoy reading in their free time generally perform better across the curriculum.","Reading for pleasure guarantees top marks in every subject.","Students achieve higher grades only in reading."],"k":1,"e":"[paraphrase / summary] Learners who enjoy reading in their free time generally perform better across the curriculum. — tend to = generally; in all subjects = across the curriculum.","h":"tend to تعني غالبًا."},{"n":6,"s":"Choose the best order for the sentences.","o":["2 – 3 – 4 – 1","2 – 4 – 3 – 1","3 – 2 – 4 – 1","2 – 3 – 1 – 4"],"x":["(1) Today, she reads at least two books every month.","(2) When Noura was younger, she rarely read for pleasure.","(3) Then a teacher gave her a novel about a girl who explored the desert.","(4) She enjoyed it so much that she began to visit the library every week."],"k":0,"e":"[best order] 2 – 3 – 4 – 1 — past → Then → result → Today.","h":"تسلسل زمني."},{"n":7,"s":"Which sentence is the best concluding sentence for the paragraph?","o":["For these reasons, parents should make reading aloud part of their daily routine.","Children's books are often colourful.","Listening is one of the four language skills.","Some parents work long hours."],"x":["Reading aloud to young children has many benefits. It builds vocabulary, improves listening skills and develops imagination. It also creates a strong bond between parents and children. ______"],"k":0,"e":"[concluding sentence] For these reasons, parents should make reading aloud part of their daily routine. — A recommendation based on the benefits.","h":"توصية مبنية على الفوائد."},{"n":8,"s":"Which word best completes the formal sentence: 'The ministry has ______ a national campaign to encourage reading.'?","o":["kicked off up","set going","launched","started up off"],"k":2,"e":"[word choice / register] launched — launched is formal and precise.","h":"launched رسمية ودقيقة."},{"n":9,"s":"The novel was so (A) interested that I (B) could not (C) stop (D) reading it.","o":["interested","could not","stop","reading"],"k":0,"e":"[error] interested — The novel causes the feeling: interesting.","h":"الرواية مثيرة: interesting."},{"n":10,"s":"Which sentence best fills the blank in the paragraph?","o":["Car journeys can be long and tiring.","Many people exercise in the evening.","Literature includes novels and poems.","They allow people to listen to books while doing other activities."],"x":["Audiobooks have become increasingly popular. ______ This makes it possible to enjoy literature during long car journeys or while exercising."],"k":3,"e":"[complete the paragraph] They allow people to listen to books while doing other activities. — This refers to listening while doing other activities.","h":"This تعود إلى الاستماع أثناء الأنشطة."},{"n":11,"s":"Which sentence is the best thesis statement for this introduction?","o":["Screens are found in almost every home.","While screens are useful for quick reading, printed texts remain better for deep understanding.","Paper is made from trees.","Reading is a popular hobby."],"x":["Many people believe that reading on screens is just as effective as reading on paper. Others are not so sure. ______"],"k":1,"e":"[topic sentence / thesis] While screens are useful for quick reading, printed texts remain better for deep understanding. — A clear, balanced, arguable position.","h":"موقف متوازن قابل للنقاش."},{"n":12,"s":"Which word or phrase best fills the blank?","o":["However","Consequently","Otherwise","Furthermore"],"x":["Libraries offer free access to thousands of books. ______, they provide quiet places to study and free workshops."],"k":3,"e":"[transition / connector] Furthermore — An additional benefit.","h":"فائدة إضافية."},{"n":13,"s":"Which sentence is written correctly?","o":["Not only do printed books last for years, but they also require no batteries.","Not only printed books last for years, but they also require no batteries.","Not only do printed books lasts for years, but they also require no batteries.","Not only printed books do last for years, but also they require no batteries."],"k":0,"e":"[error] Not only do printed books last for years, but they also require no batteries. — Not only at the start needs inversion: do + subject + base verb.","h":"Not only في البداية تحتاج قلبًا."},{"n":14,"s":"Which sentence best summarizes this paragraph?","o":["Libraries with cafés are the most popular.","People are no longer interested in libraries.","Libraries are closing because of budget cuts, but modernized libraries attract more visitors, showing that investment, not interest, is the issue.","Governments have increased library budgets."],"x":["In many countries, the number of public libraries has fallen as governments cut budgets. Yet libraries that have modernized, adding cafés, digital services and community events, have seen visitor numbers rise. This suggests that the problem is not a lack of interest but a lack of investment."],"k":2,"e":"[paraphrase / summary] Libraries are closing because of budget cuts, but modernized libraries attract more visitors, showing that investment, not interest, is the issue. — Problem + contrast + conclusion of the paragraph.","h":"المشكلة والمقابلة والخلاصة."},{"n":15,"s":"Which sentence does NOT belong in the paragraph?","o":["Sentence 3","Sentence 4","Sentence 5","Sentence 6"],"x":["(1) Writing by hand has several advantages for learners. (2) Studies show that students remember notes better when they write them by hand. (3) Handwriting also develops fine motor skills in young children. (4) Typing is usually faster than handwriting. (5) Many teachers therefore encourage students to take notes on paper. (6) Even in a digital age, the pen remains a powerful learning tool."],"k":1,"e":"[irrelevant sentence] Sentence 4 — Typing speed does not support the advantages of handwriting.","h":"سرعة الطباعة لا تدعم الفكرة."},{"n":16,"s":"The author's latest novel, (A) which (B) has been translated into twelve languages, (C) have (D) sold over a million copies.","o":["which","has been translated","have","sold"],"k":2,"e":"[error] have — The subject novel is singular: has sold.","h":"الفاعل مفرد."},{"n":17,"s":"Which word or phrase best fills the blank?","o":["Therefore","Likewise","Even so","In other words"],"x":["The book was long and difficult to read. ______, it was one of the most rewarding books I have ever read."],"k":2,"e":"[transition / connector] Even so — A concession followed by a contrasting judgement.","h":"تسليم ثم حكم مقابل."},{"n":18,"s":"Choose the best order for the sentences.","o":["2 – 3 – 4 – 1","2 – 4 – 3 – 1","3 – 2 – 4 – 1","2 – 3 – 1 – 4"],"x":["(1) This, in turn, improves their writing and their performance in exams.","(2) Regular readers meet thousands of new words every year.","(3) Over time, they learn how these words are used in different contexts.","(4) As a result, their vocabulary grows much faster than that of non-readers."],"k":0,"e":"[best order] 2 – 3 – 4 – 1 — meet words → learn use → As a result, vocabulary grows → This, in turn, improves writing.","h":"سلسلة سبب ونتيجة."},{"n":19,"s":"Which sentence is the most appropriate in a formal book review?","o":["The author does a super cool job with the main guy.","The main character is, like, really deep and stuff.","The writer totally nails the main character, no doubt.","The author develops the main character with remarkable depth and sensitivity."],"k":3,"e":"[word choice / register] The author develops the main character with remarkable depth and sensitivity. — Formal, precise evaluative language.","h":"لغة تقييم رسمية دقيقة."},{"n":20,"s":"Which sentence best concludes this essay?","o":["E-books are cheaper than printed books.","Some readers prefer magazines.","The future of reading, therefore, is likely to be shared between paper and screen.","Bookshops sell stationery as well as books."],"x":["Printed books and e-books each have their strengths. E-books are convenient and affordable, while printed books offer focus and a personal connection. Many readers now use both, depending on the situation. ______"],"k":2,"e":"[concluding sentence] The future of reading, therefore, is likely to be shared between paper and screen. — A balanced final thought matching the paragraph.","h":"فكرة ختامية متوازنة."}]},{"l":["Part B — Mixed STEP Composition Analysis (Questions 21–30)","الجزء الثاني: أسئلة متنوعة من قسم تحليل الكتابة في اختبار STEP."],"q":[{"n":21,"s":"Which sentence is the most concise?","o":["The committee will meet tomorrow.","The committee will meet together tomorrow in the future.","The committee members will gather together and meet tomorrow.","Tomorrow, the committee will have a meeting together tomorrow."],"k":0,"e":"[word choice / register] The committee will meet tomorrow. — No repeated ideas.","h":"دون تكرار."},{"n":22,"s":"Which thesis statement is the most effective for an essay about reading habits?","o":["Reading is an activity that many people do.","Schools should set aside time for free reading every day, because it builds both language skills and a lifelong love of books.","There are many kinds of books in the world.","This essay will discuss reading habits."],"k":1,"e":"[topic sentence / thesis] Schools should set aside time for free reading every day, because it builds both language skills and a lifelong love of books. — Specific, arguable and focused.","h":"محددة وقابلة للنقاش ومركزة."},{"n":23,"s":"If I (A) had known about the book fair, I (B) would have went (C) with my (D) friends.","o":["had known","would have went","with","friends"],"k":1,"e":"[error] would have went — would have + past participle: would have gone.","h":"would have gone."},{"n":24,"s":"Which word or phrase best fills the blank?","o":["so that","because","whereas","unless"],"x":["Some readers prefer fiction, ______ others choose biographies and history books."],"k":2,"e":"[transition / connector] whereas — whereas contrasts two groups.","h":"whereas للمقابلة."},{"n":25,"s":"Which sentence best paraphrases: 'The library is unlikely to close before midnight.'?","o":["The library will certainly close before midnight.","The library will probably stay open until midnight.","The library is always closed at midnight.","The library closed at midnight yesterday."],"k":1,"e":"[paraphrase / summary] The library will probably stay open until midnight. — unlikely to close before = will probably stay open until.","h":"على الأرجح سيبقى مفتوحًا."},{"n":26,"s":"Which sentence does NOT belong in the paragraph?","o":["Sentence 1","Sentence 2","Sentence 3","Sentence 4"],"x":["(1) The Riyadh International Book Fair is one of the largest in the Arab world. (2) It attracts publishers from dozens of countries. (3) Visitors can buy books in many languages. (4) Riyadh has hot summers and mild winters. (5) The fair also hosts lectures, poetry evenings and workshops."],"k":3,"e":"[irrelevant sentence] Sentence 4 — The weather does not describe the book fair.","h":"الطقس خارج الموضوع."},{"n":27,"s":"Which sentence best fills the blank in the paragraph?","o":["However, it does not take much time to rebuild this habit.","Busy schedules are common in modern life.","Children go to bed at different times.","Some families read newspapers."],"x":["Many families have stopped reading together because of busy schedules. ______ Even fifteen minutes of shared reading before bed can make a difference."],"k":0,"e":"[complete the paragraph] However, it does not take much time to rebuild this habit. — However introduces the encouraging point that the example develops.","h":"However تمهد للفكرة المشجعة."},{"n":28,"s":"Which sentence is the best concluding sentence for the paragraph?","o":["STEP is taken by many Saudi students.","Some questions are longer than others.","Writers use many different styles.","In short, preparing for this section improves both exam results and real-life communication."],"x":["Composition Analysis questions test whether students can recognize good writing. They check organization, cohesion, accuracy and style. Students who practise these skills become better readers and writers. ______"],"k":3,"e":"[concluding sentence] In short, preparing for this section improves both exam results and real-life communication. — A summary that links the exam to real life.","h":"خلاصة تربط الاختبار بالحياة."},{"n":29,"s":"Choose the best order for the sentences.","o":["2 – 4 – 3 – 1","3 – 2 – 4 – 1","2 – 3 – 4 – 1","2 – 3 – 1 – 4"],"x":["(1) Finally, review your answers if time allows.","(2) First, identify the type of question.","(3) Next, apply the strategy for that type.","(4) Then eliminate the options that are clearly wrong and choose the best answer."],"k":2,"e":"[best order] 2 – 3 – 4 – 1 — First → Next → Then → Finally.","h":"ترتيب الخطوات."},{"n":30,"s":"She (A) suggested (B) to visit the library (C) after school (D) on Thursday.","o":["suggested","to visit","after","on"],"k":1,"e":"[error] to visit — suggest is followed by -ing: suggested visiting.","h":"suggest يتبعها -ing."}]}],"n":30}],"sc":{},"review":{"quiz":[{"l":["Unit Review — 50 questions covering all six lessons of the unit. Choose the best answer (A, B, C or D).","مراجعة الوحدة: خمسون سؤالًا تغطي دروس الوحدة الستة، اختر الإجابة الصحيحة."],"q":[{"n":1,"s":"Which sentence best paraphrases: 'The bus service is likely to improve once the new depot opens.'?","o":["The bus service has already improved because of the new depot.","The new depot will definitely make the bus service worse.","The bus service caused the new depot to open.","The bus service will probably get better after the new depot starts operating."],"k":3,"e":"[paraphrase / summary · 5.2] The bus service will probably get better after the new depot starts operating. — likely to = will probably; once = after.","h":"likely تعني على الأرجح."},{"n":2,"s":"Which word or phrase best fills the blank?","o":["Nevertheless","Similarly","Consequently","For instance"],"x":["Critics say that the new stadium is too expensive. ______, it will bring international events and thousands of jobs to the city."],"k":0,"e":"[transition / connector · 5.1] Nevertheless — A rebuttal of the critics' claim.","h":"رد على النقاد."},{"n":3,"s":"The list of (A) approved books (B) were (C) sent to all schools (D) last week.","o":["approved","were","sent","last"],"k":1,"e":"[error · 5.3] were — The subject is The list (singular): was sent.","h":"الفاعل The list مفرد."},{"n":4,"s":"An essay question asks: 'Should children under twelve be allowed to own smartphones?' Which thesis answers the question most directly?","o":["Children under twelve should not own smartphones, although they may use a family device under supervision.","Smartphones have many useful applications.","Children are curious about technology.","Many adults own more than one phone."],"k":0,"e":"[topic sentence / thesis · 5.4] Children under twelve should not own smartphones, although they may use a family device under supervision. — A clear position on the exact question.","h":"موقف واضح من السؤال نفسه."},{"n":5,"s":"Which sentence does NOT belong in the paragraph?","o":["Sentence 1","Sentence 2","Sentence 3","Sentence 4"],"x":["(1) [Body 1] Cycling lanes make cities healthier. (2) People who cycle to work get regular exercise. (3) Fewer cars on the road mean cleaner air. (4) Bicycles were invented in the nineteenth century. (5) Cycling also reduces stress for many commuters."],"k":3,"e":"[irrelevant sentence · 5.5] Sentence 4 — The history of bicycles does not support the health argument.","h":"تاريخ الدراجة خارج الموضوع."},{"n":6,"s":"Which sentence is the most appropriate in a formal essay?","o":["The evidence strongly suggests that early reading has lasting benefits.","It's pretty obvious that reading early is great.","Reading early is, like, super helpful for kids.","Everybody knows early reading rocks."],"k":0,"e":"[word choice / register · 5.6] The evidence strongly suggests that early reading has lasting benefits. — Formal, evidence-based language.","h":"لغة رسمية مبنية على الأدلة."},{"n":7,"s":"Which sentence best REBUTS this argument?","o":["In fact, the internet can create genuine and supportive connections.","The internet was developed in the twentieth century.","Some people have hundreds of online contacts.","Friendship is important at every age."],"x":["It is often argued that online friendships are not real friendships. ______ Many people have formed close, lasting relationships with friends they first met online."],"k":0,"e":"[complete the paragraph · 5.1] In fact, the internet can create genuine and supportive connections. — It answers the claim directly and leads to the evidence.","h":"ترد على الادعاء مباشرة."},{"n":8,"s":"Which sentence best summarizes this paragraph?","o":["All coral reefs in the world are dying.","The Red Sea is the warmest sea in the world.","Red Sea corals appear unusually resistant to warming, and studying them may help save reefs elsewhere.","Scientists have already saved reefs worldwide."],"x":["Many coral reefs in the Red Sea have survived rising sea temperatures better than reefs elsewhere. Scientists believe these corals may be naturally adapted to warm water. They hope that studying them could help protect reefs in other parts of the world."],"k":2,"e":"[paraphrase / summary · 5.2] Red Sea corals appear unusually resistant to warming, and studying them may help save reefs elsewhere. — The main finding and its possible use.","h":"النتيجة الرئيسة واستخدامها المحتمل."},{"n":9,"s":"The manager wanted to know (A) when (B) would the report (C) be (D) ready.","o":["when","would the report","be","ready"],"k":1,"e":"[error · 5.3] would the report — An indirect question uses statement order: when the report would be ready.","h":"السؤال غير المباشر بترتيب الخبر."},{"n":10,"s":"Which sentence is the best concluding sentence for the paragraph?","o":["Some exams last for three hours.","Questions are usually numbered.","Checking answers is boring for some students.","Good time management can therefore make the difference between an average score and an excellent one."],"x":["Students who manage their time well in exams complete every question and have time to check their answers. Those who spend too long on one question often leave others unanswered. ______"],"k":3,"e":"[concluding sentence · 5.4] Good time management can therefore make the difference between an average score and an excellent one. — A conclusion drawn from the contrast.","h":"خلاصة من المقارنة."},{"n":11,"s":"Which word or phrase best fills the blank?","o":["Because of","Owing to","Despite","Thanks to"],"x":["[Body 3] ______ the advantages described above, the project has one major weakness: its cost."],"k":2,"e":"[transition / connector · 5.5] Despite — Despite + noun introduces a contrast with the earlier paragraphs.","h":"Despite للتضاد مع ما سبق."},{"n":12,"s":"Choose the best order for the sentences.","o":["2 – 3 – 4 – 1","2 – 4 – 3 – 1","3 – 2 – 4 – 1","2 – 3 – 1 – 4"],"x":["(1) Finally, they checked their answers and submitted the test.","(2) The candidates first read the instructions carefully.","(3) They then answered the questions they found easiest.","(4) After that, they returned to the more difficult ones."],"k":0,"e":"[best order · 5.6] 2 – 3 – 4 – 1 — first → then → After that → Finally.","h":"ترتيب الخطوات."},{"n":13,"s":"Which word or phrase best fills the blank?","o":["While it is true","So that it is true","Because it is true","Unless it is true"],"x":["______ that video games can be harmful, they can also teach teamwork and problem-solving."],"k":0,"e":"[transition / connector · 5.1] While it is true — A concession before the main claim.","h":"تسليم قبل الفكرة الرئيسة."},{"n":14,"s":"Which sentence best paraphrases: 'Scarcely any rain fell during the summer months.'?","o":["It rained heavily all summer.","Rain fell only at the end of the summer.","No one noticed the rain during the summer.","There was very little rain in the summer."],"k":3,"e":"[paraphrase / summary · 5.2] There was very little rain in the summer. — Scarcely any = very little.","h":"Scarcely any تعني قليلًا جدًا."},{"n":15,"s":"The more (A) carefully you plan, (B) the (C) fewest mistakes you (D) will make.","o":["carefully","the","fewest","will make"],"k":2,"e":"[error · 5.3] fewest — the more …, the + comparative: the fewer.","h":"صيغة المقارنة: the fewer."},{"n":16,"s":"Which sentence best fills the blank in the paragraph?","o":["Introductions are the first part of an essay.","Three or four sentences that end with a clear thesis are usually enough.","Some writers start with a question.","Exams are usually held in the morning."],"x":["In timed writing, the introduction should be short. ______ The rest of the time can then be spent developing the main arguments."],"k":1,"e":"[complete the paragraph · 5.4] Three or four sentences that end with a clear thesis are usually enough. — The rest of the time follows advice about a short introduction.","h":"تكملة النصيحة."},{"n":17,"s":"Which topic sentence best fits this body paragraph?","o":["Buses carry many passengers every day.","The new transport system is also environmentally friendly.","Solar panels are expensive to install.","The city has many bus stations."],"x":["[Body 2] ______ Electric buses produce no exhaust fumes, and solar panels on bus stations generate clean energy. Together, they help the city meet its environmental targets."],"k":1,"e":"[topic sentence / thesis · 5.5] The new transport system is also environmentally friendly. — It introduces the environmental details.","h":"تقدم التفاصيل البيئية."},{"n":18,"s":"Which sentence does NOT belong in the paragraph?","o":["Sentence 2","Sentence 3","Sentence 4","Sentence 5"],"x":["(1) Effective exam preparation begins weeks in advance. (2) Students should review regularly rather than all at once. (3) Practice tests help them become familiar with the format. (4) Some students prefer blue pens to black ones. (5) Adequate sleep before the exam also improves performance."],"k":2,"e":"[irrelevant sentence · 5.6] Sentence 4 — The colour of pens does not concern exam preparation.","h":"لون القلم خارج الموضوع."},{"n":19,"s":"Which sentence best concludes this argument?","o":["On balance, a sugar tax is a fair price to pay for a healthier society.","Sugar is found in many foods.","Health care is expensive in some countries.","Consumers buy many different drinks."],"x":["Some argue that a sugar tax punishes consumers. However, such taxes have reduced sugar consumption in several countries and raised money for health care. ______"],"k":0,"e":"[concluding sentence · 5.1] On balance, a sugar tax is a fair price to pay for a healthier society. — On balance gives the final position.","h":"On balance للموقف النهائي."},{"n":20,"s":"Which sentence best paraphrases: 'The museum was closed for renovation, so the trip was postponed.'?","o":["The museum was renovated because the trip was postponed.","The trip was delayed because the museum was being renovated.","The trip went ahead although the museum was closed.","The trip was cancelled permanently after the renovation."],"k":1,"e":"[paraphrase / summary · 5.2] The trip was delayed because the museum was being renovated. — so = because (reversed order, same cause).","h":"السبب والنتيجة محفوظان."},{"n":21,"s":"It is (A) vital that every student (B) attends the safety briefing (C) before (D) using the laboratory.","o":["vital","attends","before","using"],"k":1,"e":"[error · 5.3] attends — It is vital that + subject + base verb: attend.","h":"بعد vital المصدر."},{"n":22,"s":"Which word best completes the sentence in a timed essay: 'This policy would ______ benefit low-income families.'?","o":["kind of","loads","significantly","massively much"],"k":2,"e":"[word choice / register · 5.4] significantly — A formal adverb of degree.","h":"ظرف رسمي."},{"n":23,"s":"In an essay about 'reducing plastic waste', which sentence keeps the key term consistent?","o":["Increasing plastic production requires action from both shoppers and manufacturers.","Reducing plastic waste requires action from both shoppers and manufacturers.","Reducing paper waste requires action from both shoppers and manufacturers.","Recycling glass bottles requires action from both shoppers and manufacturers."],"k":1,"e":"[error · 5.5] Reducing plastic waste requires action from both shoppers and manufacturers. — The key term must stay the same throughout the essay.","h":"المصطلح الرئيس ثابت."},{"n":24,"s":"Which word or phrase best fills the blank?","o":["Therefore","Likewise","In other words","However"],"x":["The essay had a strong thesis. ______, its body paragraphs lacked evidence."],"k":3,"e":"[transition / connector · 5.6] However — A contrast between strength and weakness.","h":"تضاد بين القوة والضعف."},{"n":25,"s":"Which sentence best develops the supporters' argument?","o":["Single-sex schools are common in Saudi Arabia.","Research is carried out by universities.","Some students change schools every year.","They believe that students feel less pressure to impress others and can focus on their studies."],"x":["Supporters of single-sex schools claim that students concentrate better. ______ However, research results on this question are mixed."],"k":3,"e":"[complete the paragraph · 5.1] They believe that students feel less pressure to impress others and can focus on their studies. — The gap develops the supporters' claim before However.","h":"تطوير حجة المؤيدين."},{"n":26,"s":"Which sentence best summarizes this paragraph?","o":["Dates can be stored for months.","Because date palms met so many basic needs, they were essential to life in the Arabian desert.","Palm trees provide shade in the desert.","Refrigerators were invented in modern times."],"x":["Date palms have been grown in Arabia for thousands of years. They provide food, shade, building materials and fuel, and their fruit can be stored for months without refrigeration. For these reasons, they played a central role in desert life."],"k":1,"e":"[paraphrase / summary · 5.2] Because date palms met so many basic needs, they were essential to life in the Arabian desert. — The main idea with its general reason.","h":"الفكرة الرئيسة وسببها العام."},{"n":27,"s":"(A) Neither the teacher (B) nor the students (C) was able (D) to solve the puzzle.","o":["Neither","nor","was","to solve"],"k":2,"e":"[error · 5.3] was — With neither … nor, the verb agrees with the nearer subject (the students): were.","h":"الفعل يطابق الأقرب."},{"n":28,"s":"Choose the best order for the sentences.","o":["2 – 1 – 3 – 4","1 – 2 – 3 – 4","2 – 3 – 1 – 4","2 – 1 – 4 – 3"],"x":["(1) Next, write a thesis that answers the question directly.","(2) Begin by underlining the key words in the question.","(3) Then list two or three reasons and one counter-argument.","(4) Finally, check that each reason supports your thesis."],"k":0,"e":"[best order · 5.4] 2 – 1 – 3 – 4 — Begin → Next → Then → Finally.","h":"ترتيب خطوات التخطيط."},{"n":29,"s":"Which sentence is the best thesis statement for this introduction?","o":["Trees are planted in many countries.","Riyadh is the capital of Saudi Arabia.","Water is needed by all plants.","Large-scale tree planting can transform Saudi cities, provided that native, drought-resistant species and recycled water are used."],"x":["Many Saudi cities are planting millions of trees as part of the Green Riyadh and Saudi Green Initiative projects. Supporters say trees will cool the cities and clean the air, but others question whether there is enough water. ______"],"k":3,"e":"[topic sentence / thesis · 5.5] Large-scale tree planting can transform Saudi cities, provided that native, drought-resistant species and recycled water are used. — A clear, conditional position answering the concern.","h":"موقف مشروط يجيب عن القلق."},{"n":30,"s":"Which sentence best paraphrases: 'Few, if any, of the candidates finished early.'?","o":["Most candidates finished early.","Almost none of the candidates completed the test before the time was up.","Some candidates finished early, and others failed.","All candidates finished at the same time."],"k":1,"e":"[paraphrase / summary · 5.6] Almost none of the candidates completed the test before the time was up. — Few, if any = almost none.","h":"Few, if any تعني تقريبًا لا أحد."},{"n":31,"s":"Which word or phrase best fills the blank?","o":["As a result","In addition","Even so","For example"],"x":["Granted, the plan will take years to complete. ______, its long-term benefits justify the wait."],"k":2,"e":"[transition / connector · 5.1] Even so — A rebuttal after a concession.","h":"رد بعد التسليم."},{"n":32,"s":"Which sentence best concludes this summary?","o":["Overall, the article suggests that each format has its own place.","Paper is made from wood pulp.","Screens are found in most homes.","I personally prefer reading on my phone."],"x":["The article reports that reading on paper improves concentration and memory. It also notes that screens remain useful for quick searches and short texts. ______"],"k":0,"e":"[concluding sentence · 5.2] Overall, the article suggests that each format has its own place. — A neutral overall statement with no personal opinion.","h":"خلاصة محايدة دون رأي شخصي."},{"n":33,"s":"(A) Only after the storm (B) had passed (C) the residents were allowed to return (D) to their homes.","o":["Only","had passed","the residents were","to"],"k":2,"e":"[error · 5.3] the residents were — Only after … at the start needs inversion: were the residents.","h":"بعد Only after قلب."},{"n":34,"s":"Which sentence does NOT belong in the paragraph?","o":["Sentence 1","Sentence 2","Sentence 3","Sentence 4"],"x":["(1) Planning saves time in a writing exam. (2) A plan shows the writer which ideas to include. (3) It prevents the writer from forgetting the conclusion. (4) Exam halls are usually quiet. (5) With a plan, writers can concentrate on language while they write."],"k":3,"e":"[irrelevant sentence · 5.4] Sentence 4 — The noise level of exam halls does not concern planning.","h":"هدوء القاعة خارج الموضوع."},{"n":35,"s":"Which sentence best fills the blank in the paragraph?","o":["Vegetables are grown in many countries.","Education is a second way to promote healthy eating.","Some children dislike vegetables.","Gardens need water every day."],"x":["[Body 2] ______ For example, school gardens teach children where food comes from and encourage them to eat vegetables."],"k":1,"e":"[complete the paragraph · 5.5] Education is a second way to promote healthy eating. — For example needs a general statement before it.","h":"For example تحتاج فكرة عامة قبلها."},{"n":36,"s":"The candidate who (A) scored highest (B) on the test (C) was (D) awarding a scholarship.","o":["scored","on","was","awarding"],"k":3,"e":"[error · 5.6] awarding — Passive voice: was awarded.","h":"المبني للمجهول: was awarded."},{"n":37,"s":"Choose the best order for the sentences.","o":["2 – 1 – 3 – 4","3 – 2 – 1 – 4","2 – 3 – 1 – 4","2 – 3 – 4 – 1"],"x":["(1) However, critics point out that new roads often attract even more traffic.","(2) Some people argue that building more roads will reduce congestion.","(3) They believe wider roads allow vehicles to move faster.","(4) Investing in public transport may therefore be a better solution."],"k":2,"e":"[best order · 5.1] 2 – 3 – 1 – 4 — claim → reason → However (rebuttal) → therefore (conclusion).","h":"ادعاء ثم سبب ثم رد ثم خلاصة."},{"n":38,"s":"Which reporting verb shows that a writer gives a reason for a view?","o":["The author explains that the policy failed because it lacked funding.","The author wonders that the policy failed because it lacked funding.","The author asks that the policy failed because it lacked funding.","The author denies that the policy failed because it lacked funding."],"k":0,"e":"[word choice / register · 5.2] The author explains that the policy failed because it lacked funding. — explains that introduces a reason.","h":"explains لعرض السبب."},{"n":39,"s":"Which is the most concise version of 'The reason why the plan failed was because it was too expensive.'?","o":["The reason why the plan failed was due to the fact that it was too expensive.","The reason was because the plan was expensive, which is why it failed.","Because it was too expensive, the reason the plan failed was this.","The plan failed because it was too expensive."],"k":3,"e":"[word choice / register · 5.3] The plan failed because it was too expensive. — No repetition of reason / because.","h":"دون تكرار السبب."},{"n":40,"s":"Which word or phrase best fills the blank?","o":["Nonetheless","In contrast","Consequently","Instead"],"x":["The first draft was finished quickly. ______, there was plenty of time to check it."],"k":2,"e":"[transition / connector · 5.4] Consequently — Time to check is a result of finishing quickly.","h":"نتيجة الانتهاء السريع."},{"n":41,"s":"Tourists who (A) visit AlUla (B) is often (C) surprised by (D) the beauty of the landscape.","o":["visit","is","surprised","the"],"k":1,"e":"[error · 5.5] is — The subject Tourists is plural: are.","h":"الفاعل جمع."},{"n":42,"s":"Which thesis statement is the most effective for a STEP-style essay on social media and teenagers?","o":["Social media is used all over the world.","Teenagers have many hobbies.","There are many social media applications.","Social media can harm teenagers' sleep and self-esteem, so parents and schools should teach responsible use."],"k":3,"e":"[topic sentence / thesis · 5.6] Social media can harm teenagers' sleep and self-esteem, so parents and schools should teach responsible use. — Specific, arguable and focused.","h":"محددة وقابلة للنقاش ومركزة."},{"n":43,"s":"Which sentence does NOT belong in the paragraph?","o":["Sentence 2","Sentence 3","Sentence 4","Sentence 5"],"x":["(1) Some people argue that space exploration wastes money. (2) However, space research has produced many useful technologies. (3) Weather satellites help farmers and airlines plan ahead. (4) The Moon has no atmosphere. (5) Medical imaging also owes much to space research."],"k":2,"e":"[irrelevant sentence · 5.1] Sentence 4 — A fact about the Moon does not support the rebuttal.","h":"حقيقة عن القمر لا تدعم الرد."},{"n":44,"s":"Which sentence does NOT belong in the paragraph?","o":["Sentence 1","Sentence 2","Sentence 3","Sentence 4"],"x":["(1) A summary should be much shorter than the original text. (2) It includes only the main idea and key supporting points. (3) Examples and minor details are left out. (4) Some original texts are printed in colour. (5) The summarizer's own opinion should not appear."],"k":3,"e":"[irrelevant sentence · 5.2] Sentence 4 — Colour printing is irrelevant to summarizing.","h":"الطباعة الملونة خارج الموضوع."},{"n":45,"s":"Which sentence best fills the blank in the paragraph?","o":["Essays are usually written on paper.","It is also useful to read difficult sentences aloud.","Some sentences are very short.","Errors are common in first drafts."],"x":["When you edit, read your essay slowly, sentence by sentence. ______ This helps you notice missing words and agreement errors that your eyes may skip."],"k":1,"e":"[complete the paragraph · 5.3] It is also useful to read difficult sentences aloud. — This refers to reading aloud.","h":"This تعود إلى القراءة بصوت."},{"n":46,"s":"Which sentence best paraphrases: 'Had she started earlier, she would have finished the essay.'?","o":["She did not finish the essay because she started too late.","She started early and finished the essay.","She finished the essay although she started late.","She will finish the essay if she starts early."],"k":0,"e":"[paraphrase / summary · 5.4] She did not finish the essay because she started too late. — A third conditional: she started late and did not finish.","h":"الشرط الثالث: لم يحدث."},{"n":47,"s":"Which sentence best concludes the essay?","o":["Some trees grow very slowly.","Water is expensive to transport.","With careful planning, the green cities of the future can become a reality today.","Riyadh is located in the centre of the country."],"x":["[Conclusion] Tree planting, recycled water and native species can make Saudi cities greener and cooler without wasting precious resources. ______"],"k":2,"e":"[concluding sentence · 5.5] With careful planning, the green cities of the future can become a reality today. — A final thought consistent with the thesis.","h":"فكرة ختامية متسقة."},{"n":48,"s":"Which sentence best fills the blank in the paragraph?","o":["They choose an option that fits one sentence but not the whole paragraph.","Composition Analysis is one section of the STEP test.","Some candidates read very slowly.","Marks are given for correct answers only."],"x":["Many candidates lose marks in Composition Analysis because they read too quickly. ______ Reading the sentences before and after the gap usually reveals the correct answer."],"k":0,"e":"[complete the paragraph · 5.6] They choose an option that fits one sentence but not the whole paragraph. — The gap explains how reading too quickly causes errors.","h":"الجملة تشرح سبب الخطأ."},{"n":49,"s":"(A) Despite of the warnings, many visitors (B) continued (C) to swim (D) in the rough sea.","o":["Despite of","continued","to swim","in"],"k":0,"e":"[error · 5.3] Despite of — despite takes no of: Despite the warnings.","h":"despite بلا of."},{"n":50,"s":"Which word or phrase best fills the blank?","o":["On the contrary","Otherwise","What is more","Even though"],"x":["The candidate answered every question. ______, she had five minutes left to review her answers."],"k":2,"e":"[transition / connector · 5.6] What is more — What is more adds a further positive point.","h":"What is more للإضافة."}]}],"n":50}};
